00:10:18,952 --> 00:10:20,187
- [Joel] Now, wait a minute.

252
00:10:20,187 --> 00:10:22,723
Is it me, or did
I just lose face?

253
00:10:22,723 --> 00:10:24,792
- Meanwhile, in Illinois, U.S.A.

254
00:10:24,792 --> 00:10:26,160
(all chuckling)

255
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:28,462
♪ Gave a girl a
ride in my wagon ♪

256
00:10:28,462 --> 00:10:29,863
I love that song.

257
00:10:30,965 --> 00:10:32,333
- Someone in the Twilight Zone.

258
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:33,333
- [Tom] Look, he's
talking to the sound man

259
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:34,935
lying on the floor.

260
00:10:36,337 --> 00:10:37,405
- Wait! Wait!

261
00:10:39,573 --> 00:10:40,808
- Demi Moore?

262
00:10:40,808 --> 00:10:41,942
I've dreamed of her
running out of the woods

263
00:10:41,942 --> 00:10:43,410
into my Chevy van!

264
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,048
- Whoa!

265
00:10:48,048 --> 00:10:48,915
- [Tom] Whoa, that's Demi Moore!

266
00:10:48,915 --> 00:10:49,717
Whoa!

267
00:10:50,818 --> 00:10:52,853
- Help me, please.

268
00:10:52,853 --> 00:10:54,422
Don't wait, please.

269
00:10:54,422 --> 00:10:56,323
- I wasn't even gonna stop.

270
00:10:56,323 --> 00:10:57,290
- Whoa. You're a mess.

271
00:10:57,290 --> 00:10:59,360
Were you at Prince's house?

272
00:11:01,962 --> 00:11:03,397
- [Joel] Special guest
appearance by the car

273
00:11:03,397 --> 00:11:06,833
from "Stranded in
Space", the Fury III.

274
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:09,603
- And what a Fury it is.

275
00:11:09,603 --> 00:11:12,005
- Don't do that. I
like classical music.

276
00:11:12,005 --> 00:11:13,973
- Good. Henry likes Mozart.

277
00:11:13,973 --> 00:11:17,310
He saw "Amadeus" through
my pocket three times.

278
00:11:17,310 --> 00:11:18,812
- Henry?

279
00:11:18,812 --> 00:11:21,282
- That little guy there with
the brown fur and Fonda eyes.

280
00:11:21,282 --> 00:11:22,850
- Henry, Portrait
of a Serial Gerbil.

281
00:11:22,850 --> 00:11:25,252
(car horn honking)
- Who's this behind us?

282
00:11:25,252 --> 00:11:28,122
- [Joel] Must have got separated
from the wedding party.

283
00:11:28,122 --> 00:11:30,457
- Just get me out of here, okay?

284
00:11:30,457 --> 00:11:33,327
- Hey, Where do you get those
dash-mounted gerbil cages?

285
00:11:33,327 --> 00:11:34,595
- What does it look like?

286
00:11:34,595 --> 00:11:35,863
Please, just take
me to the airport.

287
00:11:35,863 --> 00:11:37,865
- You really must wanna
get away from this guy.

288
00:11:37,865 --> 00:11:39,133
- No, no.

289
00:11:39,133 --> 00:11:41,268
My father's airport,
Trumbull's Airfield.

290
00:11:41,268 --> 00:11:42,570
It's right on the other
side of the trees.

291
00:11:42,570 --> 00:11:43,970
You've gotta know where that is.

292
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:45,472
- Just passing through.

293
00:11:45,472 --> 00:11:46,807
- [Tom] Geez, doesn't
your dad have an airport?

294
00:11:46,807 --> 00:11:48,042
- Do you know that
guy behind us?

295
00:11:48,042 --> 00:11:49,410
- Yeah, I know him.

296
00:11:49,410 --> 00:11:50,610
- Husband or boyfriend?

297
00:11:50,610 --> 00:11:51,778
- No, he's a horn salesman.

298
00:11:51,778 --> 00:11:52,480
- I don't have
either. Look, mister?

299
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:53,847
- Max Keller.

300
00:11:53,847 --> 00:11:55,148
- Holly Trumbull.

301
00:11:55,148 --> 00:11:56,850
You're great, and
I'm really scared.

302
00:11:56,850 --> 00:11:59,187
And all I ask is just
please take me to my home.

303
00:11:59,187 --> 00:12:00,587
- Okay, okay. I'll take
you, I'll take you.

304
00:12:00,587 --> 00:12:04,492
- [Tom] Do you need a
lozenge or something?

305
00:12:04,492 --> 00:12:08,328
- [Joel] Filmed in
Mendecino County, Illinois.

306
00:12:08,328 --> 00:12:10,597
- Sorry you got into this.

307
00:12:10,597 --> 00:12:12,533
- Six more of those little
suckers going like hell.

308
00:12:12,533 --> 00:12:14,000
- You bastard!

309
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:17,070
(lively synth music)

310
00:12:18,005 --> 00:12:20,240
♪ Ain't got no rearview mirror ♪

311
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,777
(siren blaring)

312
00:12:22,777 --> 00:12:24,412
- [Joel] You know, you're kind
of a high-maintenance day,

313
00:12:24,412 --> 00:12:25,813
you know that?

314
00:12:25,813 --> 00:12:27,715
- Left out of this
damsel in distress story.

315
00:12:27,715 --> 00:12:28,782
Like, that's a cop behind us?

316
00:12:28,782 --> 00:12:29,950
- Just don't stop.

317
00:12:29,950 --> 00:12:30,785
- [Joel] Oh wow.

318
00:12:30,785 --> 00:12:32,018
- Listen, lady.

319
00:12:32,018 --> 00:12:33,253
Cops and I don't
quite snuggle up.

320
00:12:33,253 --> 00:12:34,188
- Sheriff Kyle has
a personal vendetta

321
00:12:34,188 --> 00:12:35,688
against myself and my father.

322
00:12:35,688 --> 00:12:37,223
- Vendetta?

323
00:12:37,223 --> 00:12:38,858
- Take a better look, okay?

324
00:12:38,858 --> 00:12:39,993
Do I need to spell
it out for you?

325
00:12:39,993 --> 00:12:41,695
The man tried to rape me.

326
00:12:41,695 --> 00:12:42,530
- The cop?

327
00:12:42,530 --> 00:12:43,830
(gun firing)

328
00:12:43,830 --> 00:12:44,998
- [Tom] Now he's
trying to shoot me.

329
00:12:44,998 --> 00:12:47,067
S-h-o-o-t.

330
00:12:47,067 --> 00:12:48,935
- How do I get myself
into these things?

331
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:50,337
- Pull over.

332
00:12:50,337 --> 00:12:51,672
This is the sheriff's office.

333
00:12:51,672 --> 00:12:52,507
- Office?

334
00:12:52,507 --> 00:12:54,073
That's a car.

335
00:12:54,073 --> 00:12:55,042
- Brace yourself
against the dash,

336
00:12:55,042 --> 00:12:56,443
and don't let Henry fall out.

337
00:12:56,443 --> 00:12:58,745
He gets crazy when he's mad.

338
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:02,650
♪ Here comes your TV car chase ♪

339
00:13:02,650 --> 00:13:05,552
♪ It's the TV car chase theme ♪

340
00:13:05,552 --> 00:13:08,255
♪ Your TV car chase ♪

341
00:13:08,255 --> 00:13:11,692
♪ Your TV car chase theme ♪

342
00:13:11,692 --> 00:13:12,693
Hah!

343
00:13:12,693 --> 00:13:13,527
Boogie!

344
00:13:14,695 --> 00:13:17,430
♪ TV car chase ♪

345
00:13:17,430 --> 00:13:18,432
Whoa.

346
00:13:18,432 --> 00:13:20,567
(all cheering)

347
00:13:20,567 --> 00:13:21,735
- I love that.

348
00:13:21,735 --> 00:13:25,105
- I hope Steven J.
Cannell was in that car.

349
00:13:25,105 --> 00:13:26,473
- Don't pass go, Max.

350
00:13:26,473 --> 00:13:28,142
Go directly to jail, Max.

351
00:13:28,142 --> 00:13:30,110
- Do not collect $200.

352
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:34,047
- [Tom] Only you can
prevent car explosions.

353
00:13:34,047 --> 00:13:35,648
- [Man] I thought
you died on me.

354
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:37,552
You haven't moved for an hour.

355
00:13:37,552 --> 00:13:40,087
- A warrior in
16th century Japan

356
00:13:40,087 --> 00:13:42,055
sat under an icy waterfall.

357
00:13:42,055 --> 00:13:44,758
- [Joel] He looks like
one of Henson's rats.

358
00:13:44,758 --> 00:13:47,862
- Like this, without
moving, for 86 hours.

359
00:13:47,862 --> 00:13:49,797
- Why'd he do that?

360
00:13:49,797 --> 00:13:51,765
- I can't imagine.

361
00:13:51,765 --> 00:13:54,968
- Look, I'm going for the tree
if you keep talking, old man.

362
00:13:54,968 --> 00:13:56,237
- Slow heartbeat.

363
00:13:56,237 --> 00:13:57,538
- [Tom] Seems I've
been drinking a lot.

364
00:13:57,538 --> 00:13:59,273
- Open the door of the senses.

365
00:13:59,273 --> 00:14:00,975
Listen to the silence.

366
00:14:00,975 --> 00:14:02,843
- Mind if we don't talk
for the rest of the trip?

367
00:14:02,843 --> 00:14:05,445
- You must be a lot
of laughs at a party.

368
00:14:05,445 --> 00:14:08,282
- Do you think you,
um, could stick around?

369
00:14:08,282 --> 00:14:09,917
I might need you.

370
00:14:09,917 --> 00:14:11,618
- I'm going off-duty
for the day.

371
00:14:11,618 --> 00:14:14,120
- Oh, sure. A loner, I got it.

372
00:14:15,455 --> 00:14:17,190
Sit reading the classified
ads in a local motel

373
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:19,827
until Dick Powell comes running
down the television alley

374
00:14:19,827 --> 00:14:21,662
at midnight with
a gun in one hand.

375
00:14:21,662 --> 00:14:26,267
- Ah, let Dennis Miller
do Dennis Miller, Demi.

376
00:14:26,267 --> 00:14:28,368
- Is my tummy bulging?

377
00:14:28,368 --> 00:14:31,338
- [Tom] Hey, how's
Bruce these days?

378
00:14:31,338 --> 00:14:33,773
- Um, he had his hands on me.

379
00:14:34,775 --> 00:14:35,608
Sorry.

380
00:14:36,477 --> 00:14:37,778
- That makes three of us.

381
00:14:37,778 --> 00:14:39,480
Henry was just
getting to like you.

382
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:41,948
So where's a good place
to stay around here?

383
00:14:41,948 --> 00:14:42,983
- Shallow grave.

384
00:14:42,983 --> 00:14:44,452
Train tracks are nice.

385
00:14:44,452 --> 00:14:46,687
- Clover Leaf Motel is back
down the road a couple of miles.

386
00:14:46,687 --> 00:14:48,122
- Clover Leaf?

387
00:14:48,122 --> 00:14:50,890
Maybe that'll change my luck.

388
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:52,525
So long.

389
00:14:52,525 --> 00:14:55,362
- Max, um, I believe you
can order chilled champagne

390
00:14:55,362 --> 00:14:57,163
even after midnight,

391
00:14:57,163 --> 00:15:00,700
in case Dick Powell's
company isn't enough.

392
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:01,602
- Won't be.

393
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:04,272
- What are they talking about?

394
00:15:04,272 --> 00:15:06,140
- [Tom] I have no idea.

395
00:15:09,610 --> 00:15:12,378
(Henry squeaking)

396
00:15:12,378 --> 00:15:13,847
- Don't worry.

397
00:15:13,847 --> 00:15:16,850
I'm not gonna leave this
bar through the window, pal.

398
00:15:16,850 --> 00:15:18,285
After wrecking
the sheriff's car,

399
00:15:18,285 --> 00:15:20,187
I thought I'd take a break.

400
00:15:20,187 --> 00:15:21,988
I didn't know McAllister
was right behind me.

401
00:15:21,988 --> 00:15:23,190
- [Tom] Allister McAllister?

402
00:15:23,190 --> 00:15:24,223
- [Max] You ever meet
a ninja in a bar?

403
00:15:24,223 --> 00:15:25,725
It's a lot of fun.

404
00:15:28,328 --> 00:15:32,098
- He looks about as much
like a ninja as Irene Ryan.

405
00:15:32,098 --> 00:15:33,467
Heck, it is Irene Ryan.

406
00:15:33,467 --> 00:15:35,335
(soft exotic music)

407
00:15:35,335 --> 00:15:36,837
- [Joel] You know, everybody's
gonna know he's a ninja

408
00:15:36,837 --> 00:15:39,673
if they play that theme every
time he comes in somewhere.

409
00:15:39,673 --> 00:15:43,343
- Oh, everybody's got
their own theme music.

410
00:15:45,145 --> 00:15:46,080
- [Tom] Hey, what's
a guy gotta do

411
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,715
to get beat up in this place?

412
00:15:47,715 --> 00:15:48,648
- Hey, Max.

413
00:15:48,648 --> 00:15:50,083
Max, over here.

414
00:15:50,083 --> 00:15:53,387
(upbeat country music)

415
00:15:53,387 --> 00:15:54,588
- [Joel] Hm, that's funny.

416
00:15:54,588 --> 00:15:57,357
They've quit playing
my theme music.

417
00:16:02,697 --> 00:16:06,867
- [Tom] Isn't that the guy
from "Blazing Saddles"?

418
00:16:08,035 --> 00:16:09,537
- I wanted to buy
you a drink, partner,

419
00:16:09,537 --> 00:16:11,605
for bringing Holly
back in one piece.

420
00:16:11,605 --> 00:16:13,973
Last time he blacked her eye.

421
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:16,610
Someday, someone's gonna
settle it with the sheriff.

422
00:16:16,610 --> 00:16:18,412
- By the way, who are you?

423
00:16:18,412 --> 00:16:19,780
- I'd like to do it myself.

424
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:21,148
- What'll it be?

425
00:16:21,148 --> 00:16:22,215
- At one time, a Singapore Sling

426
00:16:22,215 --> 00:16:23,650
would've been the only answer.

427
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:25,418
- [Tom] Now I want
Peanut Buster Parfait.

428
00:16:25,418 --> 00:16:27,087
- I'm looking for this person.

429
00:16:27,087 --> 00:16:28,288
- I sell drinks.

430
00:16:28,288 --> 00:16:29,723
- [Joel] Do you take
"Happenings" coupons?

431
00:16:29,723 --> 00:16:32,625
- Do you want information?
There's the sheriff right there.

432
00:16:32,625 --> 00:16:35,495
- [Joel] It's "Over the Top"!

433
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:37,463
- Hi, uh, could I talk
to you for a second?

434
00:16:37,463 --> 00:16:39,700
- No!
- That's enough, boys.

435
00:16:41,502 --> 00:16:43,103
- Oh, well. Lookit here.

436
00:16:43,103 --> 00:16:44,872
- [Tom] Yeah, size 8 petite.

437
00:16:44,872 --> 00:16:47,373
A little airport negligee, eh?

438
00:16:47,373 --> 00:16:50,343
- You know how to strut
this down the stem, old man?

439
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:51,845
Hm? (chuckling)

440
00:16:51,845 --> 00:16:54,080
- [Joel] I'll just die if
they find my Tiger Balm.

441
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:56,150
- Tres bonita, darling.

442
00:16:56,150 --> 00:16:57,650
- You may not touch that.

443
00:16:57,650 --> 00:17:00,420
- Just keeps gettin'
better, don't it?

444
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:03,257
- I've been hearing about
him down at the truck stop.

445
00:17:03,257 --> 00:17:04,592
- [Joel] It's a
ninja truck stop.

446
00:17:04,592 --> 00:17:06,393
- That old man can
take care of himself.

447
00:17:06,393 --> 00:17:08,962
- Yeah, well, the sheriff
and I have a prior.

448
00:17:08,962 --> 00:17:10,130
- Go for it, kid.

449
00:17:10,130 --> 00:17:11,432
Hard and fast.

450
00:17:11,432 --> 00:17:14,033
(upbeat music)

451
00:17:17,137 --> 00:17:18,072
(Max shouting)

452
00:17:18,072 --> 00:17:21,040
- [Tom] Out you pixies go!

453
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,708
Liar! You liar, you!

454
00:17:25,778 --> 00:17:26,947
- That's enough!

455
00:17:26,947 --> 00:17:28,115
That's enough!

456
00:17:28,115 --> 00:17:30,083
Let's get that loudmouth.

457
00:17:30,083 --> 00:17:31,585
- [Tom] Which one?

458
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:38,092
(all cheering)

459
00:17:38,092 --> 00:17:41,162
- [Joel] Hey, must be
a health inspector.

460
00:17:41,162 --> 00:17:41,995
Tilt.

461
00:17:44,030 --> 00:17:45,365
- Hey, look, if you
lost your quarter,

462
00:17:45,365 --> 00:17:47,367
just fill out a form and, oh.

463
00:17:47,367 --> 00:17:51,105
- [Tom] What do we do
with these here tokens?

464
00:17:52,605 --> 00:17:53,940
Good thing I'm not
a cigarette machine.

465
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:58,678
This guy woulda kicked
my butt. (chuckling)

466
00:17:58,678 --> 00:18:02,148
- 8 ball, corner, well,
you know the rest.

467
00:18:04,652 --> 00:18:07,453
- [Joel] Hey, uh,
it unscrews. Aw.

468
00:18:12,525 --> 00:18:14,093
- [Tom] This rules.

469
00:18:16,597 --> 00:18:20,300
- [Joel] Oh, it started
falling before he kicked it.

470
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:22,102
- Hey, was that necessary?

471
00:18:22,102 --> 00:18:22,937
Look, Lee.

472
00:18:22,937 --> 00:18:23,870
We made some mistakes.

473
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:25,772
You made some mistakes.

474
00:18:27,473 --> 00:18:28,908
- I need your help.

475
00:18:28,908 --> 00:18:31,678
- [Joel] Hey, I got
some tools in my truck.

476
00:18:31,678 --> 00:18:33,247
- Ever think of hiring
out as a tornado?

477
00:18:33,247 --> 00:18:34,948
- Just get me outta here.

478
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:37,117
- [Joel] Man, is he hammy.

479
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:43,390
- [Tom] Hey, it smells like
urine and cedar chips in here.

480
00:18:43,390 --> 00:18:45,425
- Let's beat cheeks.
Little tiny ones.

481
00:18:45,425 --> 00:18:48,328
(suspenseful music)

482
00:18:48,328 --> 00:18:49,162
- Crazy.

483
00:18:51,498 --> 00:18:54,167
- [Tom] Dun-dun-dun dun-dun dun.

484
00:18:54,167 --> 00:18:56,603
- Do you always carry an arsenal
with you everywhere you go?

485
00:18:56,603 --> 00:18:57,770
- You always carry a hamster?

486
00:18:57,770 --> 00:18:59,707
- All my possessions
are with me.

487
00:18:59,707 --> 00:19:02,442
Some are more
lethal than others.

488
00:19:02,442 --> 00:19:04,110
- I was in a bar
one time in Saigon.

489
00:19:04,110 --> 00:19:05,945
- [Tom] Yeah, right.
When you were a baby.

490
00:19:05,945 --> 00:19:07,247
- This young dude comes and
tears the place to pieces,

491
00:19:07,247 --> 00:19:08,715
like it was made outta nothing.

492
00:19:08,715 --> 00:19:11,485
- I'll get out right here.
- Said he was a ninja.

493
00:19:11,485 --> 00:19:13,020
- A ninja?

494
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:14,487
- Yeah, he carried a variety
of different little weapons

495
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:15,822
in a leather pouch.

496
00:19:15,822 --> 00:19:17,925
- Oh, that's a chiropodist.

497
00:19:17,925 --> 00:19:19,425
- [Joel] Hm?

498
00:19:19,425 --> 00:19:21,160
- Hey, what else you got
in that suitcase of yours?

499
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,395
- My toothbrush.

500
00:19:22,395 --> 00:19:23,797
- [Joel] Which could
rip a man's teeth out.

501
00:19:23,797 --> 00:19:24,998
- How could you be hurt?

502
00:19:24,998 --> 00:19:27,367
I mean, no one
even came near you.

503
00:19:27,367 --> 00:19:28,868
- Shuriken wound.

504
00:19:28,868 --> 00:19:32,005
It's a small spiked wheel
in the small of my back.

505
00:19:32,005 --> 00:19:33,973
Keeps reopening.

506
00:19:33,973 --> 00:19:35,242
- We better stay out
of the emergency rooms

507
00:19:35,242 --> 00:19:36,977
till the sheriff gets
tired of watching 'em.

508
00:19:36,977 --> 00:19:37,912
- [Tom] Yeah, and you'd better

509
00:19:37,912 --> 00:19:39,680
take the wheel out of your back.

510
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,848
- Find someplace else.

511
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:43,583
- You little dickens.

512
00:19:43,583 --> 00:19:44,585
- Your home?

513
00:19:45,785 --> 00:19:47,120
- You're traveling in it, Jack.

514
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:50,357
- [Tom] You're jacking
in it, Traveler.

515
00:19:52,258 --> 00:19:54,595
- Mr. Trumbull, any one
of my client's proposals

516
00:19:54,595 --> 00:19:56,230
would make you a
very wealthy man.

517
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:57,530
- It's Claude Akins, and
he's got his ape mask!

518
00:19:57,530 --> 00:19:59,432
Oh no. It's just Claude.

519
00:19:59,432 --> 00:20:00,400
- Buy yourself LaGuardia.

520
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:02,035
- Eh. Coach would be cheaper.

521
00:20:02,035 --> 00:20:04,170
- In my office there's
a picture of a field

522
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:06,205
with a jenny sitting in it.

523
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:09,308
- [Tom] That's that
Wyeth painting.

524
00:20:09,308 --> 00:20:12,178
- A man in a leather flying
jacket wearing a red scarf.

525
00:20:12,178 --> 00:20:13,780
He's got his arm around the
shoulder of another man.

526
00:20:13,780 --> 00:20:15,015
- [Joel] Oh, Tom Selleck.

527
00:20:15,015 --> 00:20:17,918
- You know where that
field is, Mr. Havilland?

528
00:20:17,918 --> 00:20:20,820
- You've caused my client
to lose a lot of money.

529
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:22,422
- A William Daniels wannabe.

530
00:20:22,422 --> 00:20:23,390
- Unnecessary grief.

531
00:20:23,390 --> 00:20:25,025
- That field's right here,

532
00:20:25,025 --> 00:20:26,493
and the man in the
leather flying jacket

533
00:20:26,493 --> 00:20:28,262
wearing a red scarf,
that's my father.

534
00:20:28,262 --> 00:20:29,562
- Oh, it was a trick question.

535
00:20:29,562 --> 00:20:31,998
- The older man with the biplane

536
00:20:31,998 --> 00:20:33,567
was a fellow named
Wilbur Wright,

537
00:20:33,567 --> 00:20:35,068
who'd gone to have
lunch with my father

538
00:20:35,068 --> 00:20:36,537
because he'd invented
a little thing called

539
00:20:36,537 --> 00:20:38,938
a turn and bank indicator.

540
00:20:38,938 --> 00:20:40,773
Now, Mr. Wright
thought that this

541
00:20:40,773 --> 00:20:43,077
should be a good place
to build an airport.

542
00:20:43,077 --> 00:20:44,543
- Bad place to film a movie.

543
00:20:44,543 --> 00:20:46,780
- And my father thought so too.

544
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:48,282
- I can assure you that--

545
00:20:48,282 --> 00:20:49,783
- [Tom] I have no clue
what you're talking about.

546
00:20:49,783 --> 00:20:51,752
- If Mr. Christensen
would like to come by here

547
00:20:51,752 --> 00:20:54,988
and take a plane ride,
it's on the house.

548
00:20:54,988 --> 00:20:56,255
- [Joel] Oh, he's gonna
stab him in the throat

549
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:57,958
like "Godfather III".

550
00:20:57,958 --> 00:20:59,558
- Maybe he'd have a
better perspective

551
00:20:59,558 --> 00:21:01,862
of the world from 5000 feet.

552
00:21:03,697 --> 00:21:06,032
- Those lenses cost
me a lot of money.

553
00:21:06,032 --> 00:21:07,467
Please, be very careful--

554
00:21:07,467 --> 00:21:09,937
- Oh. I thought he was
gonna rip off his mustache.

555
00:21:09,937 --> 00:21:11,805
- Every time I fly
into this airport

556
00:21:11,805 --> 00:21:13,040
I look down through the clouds.

557
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:14,675
- [Tom] And I spit.

558
00:21:14,675 --> 00:21:17,277
- And I see some good memories.

559
00:21:18,412 --> 00:21:21,882
They wouldn't look that
good any place else.

560
00:21:23,183 --> 00:21:24,818
And you tell Mr.
Christensen that.

561
00:21:24,818 --> 00:21:28,855
- [Joel] Mr. Christensen,
hoist the main sail!

562
00:21:28,855 --> 00:21:29,857
- Very well.

563
00:21:31,325 --> 00:21:34,127
- Ooh! With the oh, thank
you very much, Mr. Doyle.

564
00:21:34,127 --> 00:21:35,928
- [Tom] Claude Akins, ladies
and gentlemen, Claude Akins.

565
00:21:35,928 --> 00:21:36,930
Let's give him a big hand.

566
00:21:36,930 --> 00:21:39,598
He'll be back later in the show.

567
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:41,802
- [Joel] You know,
say what you want,

568
00:21:41,802 --> 00:21:44,137
but Claude Akins
has a nice rump.

569
00:21:44,137 --> 00:21:45,705
- [Tom] Boy, don't he though?

570
00:21:45,705 --> 00:21:47,373
- You guys talking
about my butt?

571
00:21:47,373 --> 00:21:48,742
- D'oh!
- Yeah, you crack me up.

572
00:21:48,742 --> 00:21:49,977
I've seen the show.

573
00:21:49,977 --> 00:21:52,478
- Thought you might
need some help.

574
00:21:52,478 --> 00:21:55,182
There's a run on old guys
getting tough tonight.

575
00:21:55,182 --> 00:21:56,783
- What're you doing back here?

576
00:21:56,783 --> 00:21:58,418
- Who's Christensen?
- Property owner.

577
00:21:58,418 --> 00:22:00,120
Owns as much of this town
as the law will allow.

578
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:01,822
- Ah, the character
meeting place.

579
00:22:01,822 --> 00:22:02,855
- Shopping center.

580
00:22:02,855 --> 00:22:04,323
- Just stay out of this, Holly.

581
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:06,158
- Got into some more
trouble, and brought it back.

582
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:08,428
Some old guy the
sheriff was hassling.

583
00:22:08,428 --> 00:22:10,163
- All the way from town, huh?

584
00:22:10,163 --> 00:22:11,398
(siren blaring)

585
00:22:11,398 --> 00:22:12,765
- [Tom] Someone's
broken ape law.

586
00:22:12,765 --> 00:22:14,133
- My van.

587
00:22:14,133 --> 00:22:15,435
- Take him to the PQ.

588
00:22:15,435 --> 00:22:17,270
- Get him a Dilly Bar.

589
00:22:22,675 --> 00:22:25,312
- [Joel] Mr. Akins, deputy
wanted to see your butt.

590
00:22:25,312 --> 00:22:26,547
- [Kyle] Start
searching over there.

591
00:22:26,547 --> 00:22:27,880
- You got a warrant, sheriff?

592
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:30,150
- [Tom] Yeah, got a
made-for-TV warrant right here.

593
00:22:30,150 --> 00:22:31,685
- Because you better have one
before you take one more step

594
00:22:31,685 --> 00:22:34,855
onto my tarmac, and a
stretcher to take you off.

595
00:22:34,855 --> 00:22:36,990
- Threatening an officer of
the law is a serious offense.

596
00:22:36,990 --> 00:22:38,725
- You're not listening to me!

597
00:22:38,725 --> 00:22:41,227
Now you get off my property!

598
00:22:41,227 --> 00:22:43,197
- [Joel] Man's gotta know
his limitations, Clint.

599
00:22:43,197 --> 00:22:45,965
- [Kyle] All I'm gonna need
is one more FAA entrenchment,

600
00:22:45,965 --> 00:22:48,602
and I'll be back
to shut you down.

601
00:22:48,602 --> 00:22:49,702
Chew on that.

602
00:22:51,270 --> 00:22:52,338
- What happened?

603
00:22:52,338 --> 00:22:53,173
Kyle?

604
00:22:53,173 --> 00:22:54,440
- Who's Kyle?

605
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:55,542
- He's hurt.

606
00:22:55,542 --> 00:22:57,043
- [Holly] Who is he?

607
00:22:57,043 --> 00:22:58,312
- I'd like to know the
answer to that one myself.

608
00:22:58,312 --> 00:22:59,278
- [Tom] He's the Ugly.

609
00:22:59,278 --> 00:23:00,013
- [Joel] No, he's the Bad.

610
00:23:00,013 --> 00:23:00,847
- [Tom] Oh.

611
00:23:00,847 --> 00:23:02,148
- See you later?

612
00:23:05,952 --> 00:23:07,220
- [Tom] Ooh.

613
00:23:07,220 --> 00:23:08,755
Lotta electricity in
that, I'll tell you.

614
00:23:08,755 --> 00:23:11,492
- Wow. He got paid
to kiss Demi Moore.

615
00:23:11,492 --> 00:23:13,393
- [Tom] Most people have.

616
00:23:13,393 --> 00:23:14,928
Ooh.

617
00:23:14,928 --> 00:23:16,497
- Did she kiss you?

618
00:23:19,165 --> 00:23:20,500
- This guy.

619
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:22,702
- Seemed like the right moment.

620
00:23:22,702 --> 00:23:23,737
- [Tom] D'oh!

621
00:23:24,905 --> 00:23:25,972
- Guess they're just
not making ninjas

622
00:23:25,972 --> 00:23:27,340
the way they used to, huh.

623
00:23:27,340 --> 00:23:28,475
- Guess not.
- What a burn.

624
00:23:28,475 --> 00:23:29,877
- What do you know of the ninja?

625
00:23:29,877 --> 00:23:34,180
- Well, my uncle in Milawukee's
best friend is a ninja.

626
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:38,418
- You know, I'm surprised
your fellow ninjas let you go.

627
00:23:38,418 --> 00:23:39,920
- There was a send-off.

628
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:41,588
- Yeah, pinwheel in the back.

629
00:23:41,588 --> 00:23:42,522
Nice.

630
00:23:42,522 --> 00:23:43,423
Max Keller.

631
00:23:45,225 --> 00:23:46,760
Do I get to call you Master?

632
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:47,760
- It's got a ring to it.

633
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:49,728
- [Tom] Yeah, so does a bathtub.

634
00:23:49,728 --> 00:23:51,998
- John Peter McAllister is
the name on the discharge.

635
00:23:51,998 --> 00:23:53,533
- From where?

636
00:23:53,533 --> 00:23:54,500
They don't teach what you
did in any army I know of.

637
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:56,068
- Army Air Corps.

638
00:23:56,068 --> 00:23:58,505
At the end of the war I
found myself in Japan,

639
00:23:58,505 --> 00:23:59,940
a ticket home,
and nowhere to go.

640
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:01,207
- Why didn't you go home?

641
00:24:01,207 --> 00:24:03,075
- Something about
the tranquility.

642
00:24:03,075 --> 00:24:05,245
- [Joel] The tranquility
of postwar Japan?

643
00:24:05,245 --> 00:24:07,113
(Tom chuckling)

644
00:24:07,113 --> 00:24:08,882
- What brought you home?

645
00:24:08,882 --> 00:24:10,383
Or were you just running?

646
00:24:10,383 --> 00:24:12,918
- You know, this scene is
really faithful to the book.

647
00:24:12,918 --> 00:24:14,020
- [Tom] It shows.

648
00:24:14,020 --> 00:24:14,955
- My daughter.

649
00:24:14,955 --> 00:24:16,288
One I didn't even know I had.

650
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,557
- [Tom] Her name's Lefty.

651
00:24:17,557 --> 00:24:20,227
Wrote to me a month
ago from Ellerston.

652
00:24:20,227 --> 00:24:23,497
- This picture's taken outside
of one of Trumbull's hangars.

653
00:24:23,497 --> 00:24:25,898
- [Joel] Uh, why's she
handcuffed to a biplane?

654
00:24:25,898 --> 00:24:27,733
- And that's why you've traveled
halfway around the world

655
00:24:27,733 --> 00:24:29,402
after 30 years?

656
00:24:29,402 --> 00:24:30,603
Just to find her?

657
00:24:30,603 --> 00:24:32,072
- What other reason
could there be?

658
00:24:32,072 --> 00:24:34,307
- [Tom] World perks card,
frequent flyer miles.

659
00:24:34,307 --> 00:24:37,010
- You're looking over
your shoulder for someone.

660
00:24:37,010 --> 00:24:38,278
Secrets locked inside your head

661
00:24:38,278 --> 00:24:39,712
that no one else can know about?

662
00:24:39,712 --> 00:24:41,682
- Lots of secrets.

663
00:24:41,682 --> 00:24:44,083
- I'll take the
ones you can give.

664
00:24:44,083 --> 00:24:45,452
(chair scraping)
- [Tom] Ah!

665
00:24:45,452 --> 00:24:46,787
- Sounded like his
stitches were ripping.

666
00:24:46,787 --> 00:24:47,587
[Tom] Oof.

667
00:24:47,587 --> 00:24:48,555
- I don't understand.

668
00:24:48,555 --> 00:24:50,557
- I'm making a deal with you.

669
00:24:50,557 --> 00:24:52,658
I'll help you find your daughter

670
00:24:52,658 --> 00:24:55,862
if you'll teach me what
you did in that bar.

671
00:24:55,862 --> 00:24:58,097
I mean, the way you
moved, the way you felt!

672
00:24:58,097 --> 00:24:59,565
- [Tom] The way
you sang off-key!

673
00:24:59,565 --> 00:25:01,300
- There's all kinds of tricks
in that suitcase of yours.

674
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:03,102
- You would not
endure the discipline.

675
00:25:03,102 --> 00:25:04,270
- [Max] Try me!

676
00:25:04,270 --> 00:25:05,872
- Or the emotional commitment.

677
00:25:05,872 --> 00:25:07,440
- What, what, you don't
think I got emotions?

678
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:08,808
- Too many of them.

679
00:25:08,808 --> 00:25:10,777
- [Joel] You're
practically Leo Buscaglia.

680
00:25:10,777 --> 00:25:12,845
- Take on six attackers at once.

681
00:25:12,845 --> 00:25:14,513
That's not where it is, Max.

682
00:25:14,513 --> 00:25:15,848
- I can hack it.

683
00:25:15,848 --> 00:25:17,183
- You've got nice qualities.

684
00:25:17,183 --> 00:25:18,252
- [Joel] Strong cheekbones.

685
00:25:18,252 --> 00:25:20,920
- But not for a ninja.

686
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:22,855
Anyway I'm a
cantankerous old man,

687
00:25:22,855 --> 00:25:24,323
who's lived alone
a lot of years.

688
00:25:24,323 --> 00:25:26,358
- [Tom] And I'm gonna learn
the true meaning of Christmas.

689
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:27,693
- I can see why.

690
00:25:29,963 --> 00:25:31,530
I've been alone too.

691
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:32,798
- [Tom] Aww.

692
00:25:32,798 --> 00:25:34,833
- Just thought I'd
try another route.

693
00:25:34,833 --> 00:25:35,968
- [Joel] Another paper route.

694
00:25:35,968 --> 00:25:37,237
- [Tom] Yeah.

695
00:25:37,237 --> 00:25:39,907
- Anyway, hang in
there, old fella.

696
00:25:39,907 --> 00:25:41,708
- I'll hang in.

697
00:25:41,708 --> 00:25:43,377
- Good luck finding
your daughter.

698
00:25:43,377 --> 00:25:45,145
- Go to bed, old man!

699
00:25:47,580 --> 00:25:51,183
- [Tom] This dialogue was
lifted from "Then Came Bronson".

700
00:25:51,183 --> 00:25:54,020
Don't you think?
- Say hi to Dick.

701
00:25:55,255 --> 00:25:57,223
- Good luck finding yourself.

702
00:25:57,223 --> 00:25:59,993
- What? Did you say something?

703
00:25:59,993 --> 00:26:02,695
- [Tom] When
Mummenschanz goes bad.

704
00:26:02,695 --> 00:26:05,332
(ominous music)

705
00:26:09,902 --> 00:26:10,737
- [Joel] Uh, no.

706
00:26:10,737 --> 00:26:13,105
It goes in, in the tank.

707
00:26:13,105 --> 00:26:13,940
No.

708
00:26:15,042 --> 00:26:15,942
- That's enough.

709
00:26:15,942 --> 00:26:18,043
Get to the hangar.

710
00:26:18,043 --> 00:26:19,112
- Cold, cold.

711
00:26:20,213 --> 00:26:22,448
You're nowhere near the tank.

712
00:26:22,448 --> 00:26:23,883
Warmer.

713
00:26:23,883 --> 00:26:27,887
- [Tom] Here's Katherine
Hepburn gassing up her plane.

714
00:26:27,887 --> 00:26:30,790
(melancholy music)

715
00:26:37,530 --> 00:26:40,100
(Henry squeaking)
(Tom gasping)

716
00:26:40,100 --> 00:26:42,235
- Guess nobody wants us, Henry.

717
00:26:42,235 --> 00:26:46,472
- [Joel] This is the
dark night of our souls.

718
00:26:46,472 --> 00:26:49,308
(engine starting)

719
00:26:55,315 --> 00:26:58,318
(suspenseful music)

720
00:26:59,485 --> 00:27:02,222
- Ow, ow, ow, ow,
ow, ow, ow, ow.

721
00:27:07,993 --> 00:27:09,595
- [Holly] Bye, Max.

722
00:27:13,733 --> 00:27:15,235
- [Tom] Ooh.

723
00:27:15,235 --> 00:27:16,435
Flames.

724
00:27:16,435 --> 00:27:18,772
- [Joel] Is that
Mrs. O'Leary's barn?

725
00:27:18,772 --> 00:27:22,042
- Looks like Edie Sedgwick
fell asleep again.

726
00:27:22,042 --> 00:27:23,943
- [Tom] Oh, and speaking of
flaming, it's about time to go.

727
00:27:23,943 --> 00:27:25,345
- I've got things to do.

728
00:27:25,345 --> 00:27:26,947
- Did you know that actresses-
- Where's Crow going?

729
00:27:26,947 --> 00:27:28,948
- You know, actresses always
run into a flaming building.

730
00:27:28,948 --> 00:27:30,450
Hey, Crow, come back!

731
00:27:30,450 --> 00:27:31,283
Hey.

732
00:27:43,128 --> 00:27:45,232
Hey, little circuit guy.
What are you working on?

733
00:27:45,232 --> 00:27:47,467
You kind of left the theater
in a hurry, you know.

734
00:27:47,467 --> 00:27:48,768
- Yeah, what's the
hoodoo, skitter?

735
00:27:48,768 --> 00:27:50,170
- Hey, uh, dim the lights, guys.

736
00:27:50,170 --> 00:27:51,337
I got something to show you.

737
00:27:51,337 --> 00:27:53,072
Uh, Cambot, play some of that

738
00:27:53,072 --> 00:27:55,475
appropriately tension-filled
incidental music.

739
00:27:55,475 --> 00:27:58,043
- What's this all about?

740
00:27:58,043 --> 00:27:59,445
- We can't talk here.

741
00:27:59,445 --> 00:28:01,748
- Crow, aren't you being
just a bit overdramatic?

742
00:28:01,748 --> 00:28:02,982
- Well, sure.

743
00:28:02,982 --> 00:28:04,550
But I've stumbled upon
a plot that once exposed

744
00:28:04,550 --> 00:28:08,053
will blow the lid off the
entertainment industry.

745
00:28:08,053 --> 00:28:10,090
Did either of you two stop
to consider for a moment

746
00:28:10,090 --> 00:28:12,792
why Timothy Van Patten
is in this stupid film?

747
00:28:12,792 --> 00:28:14,460
- Uh, Patrick Swayze was busy?

748
00:28:14,460 --> 00:28:16,028
- Good guess, but
I thought of that.

749
00:28:16,028 --> 00:28:17,797
No, we're dealing with
something even more terrifying

750
00:28:17,797 --> 00:28:19,698
than the Swayze conundrum.

751
00:28:19,698 --> 00:28:21,902
I'm talking about a
plot more insidious.

752
00:28:21,902 --> 00:28:25,037
Gentlemen, I present
for your consideration,

753
00:28:25,037 --> 00:28:27,640
assist, the Van Patten Project!

754
00:28:28,975 --> 00:28:30,977
Sitting stop the Van
Patten corporate structure,

755
00:28:30,977 --> 00:28:32,645
Dick Van Patten,
or should I say,

756
00:28:32,645 --> 00:28:35,582
Don Dick Van Vito
Patten Corleone!

757
00:28:35,582 --> 00:28:38,217
His evil plan, to place
an annoyingly bad actor,

758
00:28:38,217 --> 00:28:41,320
preferably one of his own
hellish drop, in every B grade,

759
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:43,457
made-for-TV and low-budget
film in Hollywood.

760
00:28:43,457 --> 00:28:46,192
- Uh, that would be
all of them. (laughing)

761
00:28:46,192 --> 00:28:48,127
- (clearing throat) His
plan is quite simple.

762
00:28:48,127 --> 00:28:50,097
He begins his career
with the Lunts,

763
00:28:50,097 --> 00:28:51,932
gadding about in
legitimate theater.

764
00:28:51,932 --> 00:28:53,132
Then he snatches a plum role

765
00:28:53,132 --> 00:28:55,067
in the television sitcom "Mama".

766
00:28:55,067 --> 00:28:56,937
The popular show runs until '56,

767
00:28:56,937 --> 00:28:59,738
then, mysteriously, no Dick.

768
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:02,042
Fade to the '70s,
decade of shame,

769
00:29:02,042 --> 00:29:04,043
Dick explodes across the
television screen with shows

770
00:29:04,043 --> 00:29:06,312
like "The New Dick Van Dyke
Show" and "The Partners",

771
00:29:06,312 --> 00:29:08,013
"When Things Were Rotten",
and "Eight Is Enough",

772
00:29:08,013 --> 00:29:09,815
a show that launched
the criminal career

773
00:29:09,815 --> 00:29:11,683
of many a young hack talent.

774
00:29:11,683 --> 00:29:12,952
- [Joel] Uh-huh.

775
00:29:12,952 --> 00:29:14,387
- Now, Timothy Van
Patten comes forth

776
00:29:14,387 --> 00:29:15,655
to do his evil in "The
White Shadow", "The Master".

777
00:29:15,655 --> 00:29:17,090
Then James Van Patten
gets a small role

778
00:29:17,090 --> 00:29:18,792
in the short-lived
western, "The Chisholms".

779
00:29:18,792 --> 00:29:20,025
And then what happens to him?

780
00:29:20,025 --> 00:29:21,260
I don't know!

781
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:22,462
And then there's
Vincent, Vincent,

782
00:29:22,462 --> 00:29:23,963
who is truly abysmal
in "Apple's Way"

783
00:29:23,963 --> 00:29:25,665
and "Three for the Road",
then became the Bionic Boy.

784
00:29:25,665 --> 00:29:27,167
At least he could
smell the bacon frying

785
00:29:27,167 --> 00:29:28,635
and had the good sense to
become a tennis player!

786
00:29:28,635 --> 00:29:31,972
The parallels with "The
Godfather" are inescapable.

787
00:29:31,972 --> 00:29:34,040
- Sad when it happens to
somebody you know, isn't it?

788
00:29:34,040 --> 00:29:35,007
- I know.

789
00:29:35,007 --> 00:29:36,408
- Enter Joyce Van Patten.

790
00:29:36,408 --> 00:29:37,677
Yes, Joyce, sister of Dick,

791
00:29:37,677 --> 00:29:39,112
the real power behind
the Van Patten empire.

792
00:29:39,112 --> 00:29:40,747
Joyce, like Caligula's
grandmother,

793
00:29:40,747 --> 00:29:41,882
plotting and planning
in the background,

794
00:29:41,882 --> 00:29:43,348
a string of failures
in her wake!

795
00:29:43,348 --> 00:29:45,818
"The Don Rickles Show",
"The Mary Tyler Moore Hour",

796
00:29:45,818 --> 00:29:49,155
"The Good Guys", with Herb
Edelman and Bob Denver,

797
00:29:49,155 --> 00:29:50,657
a show I actually kind of liked

798
00:29:50,657 --> 00:29:53,292
except for the third season
when Rufus got rid of the taxi,

799
00:29:53,292 --> 00:29:54,527
and helped out
more in the diner.

800
00:29:54,527 --> 00:29:55,995
You know, because then
it really kind of--

801
00:29:55,995 --> 00:29:59,398
- Crow, Crow would you
please get to your point?

802
00:29:59,398 --> 00:30:01,267
- Uh, I don't have one.

803
00:30:01,267 --> 00:30:02,568
- That's great.

804
00:30:02,568 --> 00:30:04,570
Okay, c'mon. You're
coming with me.

805
00:30:04,570 --> 00:30:06,472
- Whoa! Whoa!

806
00:30:06,472 --> 00:30:08,575
- We'll be right
back after this.

807
00:30:08,575 --> 00:30:11,177
(upbeat music)

808
00:30:14,413 --> 00:30:16,048
- Then we'll be building
from Willow Lane

809
00:30:16,048 --> 00:30:18,952
right across the airport.
- [Tom] Oh, fun, huh?

810
00:30:18,952 --> 00:30:19,785
- Congratulations, Johnny.

811
00:30:19,785 --> 00:30:20,987
It's gonna be a beauty.

812
00:30:20,987 --> 00:30:23,222
(slurping)

813
00:30:24,090 --> 00:30:25,592
(gulping)

814
00:30:25,592 --> 00:30:27,993
(burping)

815
00:30:27,993 --> 00:30:30,230
- Wonderful party,
Mr. Christensen.

816
00:30:30,230 --> 00:30:32,332
- [Joel] TV's Tony Danza.

817
00:30:33,633 --> 00:30:35,735
- So what do you think?

818
00:30:35,735 --> 00:30:37,737
- I think your shopping
center is premature,

819
00:30:37,737 --> 00:30:39,705
considering you don't
own the ground yet.

820
00:30:39,705 --> 00:30:41,540
- Yeah, well, so are you.

821
00:30:41,540 --> 00:30:42,908
- And how did it go down?

822
00:30:42,908 --> 00:30:44,477
- It didn't go down,
Mr. Christensen.

823
00:30:44,477 --> 00:30:45,945
- [Tom] How did you hear that?

824
00:30:45,945 --> 00:30:48,380
- Like a big fireball.

825
00:30:48,380 --> 00:30:52,018
- I'm sorry, I'm afraid I, I
don't understand your remark.

826
00:30:52,018 --> 00:30:53,587
- Maybe you can understand this.

827
00:30:53,587 --> 00:30:55,153
You're dealing with
real people here.

828
00:30:55,153 --> 00:30:56,622
- With Skiff Stevenston?

829
00:30:56,622 --> 00:30:58,123
- The kind that builds
things and cares about them.

830
00:30:58,123 --> 00:30:59,525
And can't be bought like
your Harvard flunky here.

831
00:30:59,525 --> 00:31:00,760
- D'oh!
- Go ahead.

832
00:31:00,760 --> 00:31:02,828
Blow up another airplane.

833
00:31:02,828 --> 00:31:04,330
Set fire to the
whole damn airport.

834
00:31:04,330 --> 00:31:05,565
Because you're not gonna
move Trumbull or his daughter

835
00:31:05,565 --> 00:31:06,967
four feet off that
patch of earth!

836
00:31:06,967 --> 00:31:08,935
Not if I can help it.
- Way to stick it to the man!

837
00:31:08,935 --> 00:31:11,503
(all whistling and applauding)

838
00:31:11,503 --> 00:31:13,138
- That's not a
familiar name to me.

839
00:31:13,138 --> 00:31:16,175
- Here's a name to get
familiar with. Max Keller.

840
00:31:16,175 --> 00:31:17,510
It's mine, and I want
you to get used to it

841
00:31:17,510 --> 00:31:19,145
because you're gonna
be hearing it a lot.

842
00:31:19,145 --> 00:31:20,647
Probably down at
the DA's office.

843
00:31:20,647 --> 00:31:22,882
- [Tom] Because all the DAs
are named Max Keller now.

844
00:31:22,882 --> 00:31:25,050
- You're not on the
guest list, Mr. Keller.

845
00:31:25,050 --> 00:31:27,420
- Long line of party crashers.

846
00:31:27,420 --> 00:31:29,088
- Mr. Keller walked
into the wrong party.

847
00:31:29,088 --> 00:31:30,523
See him out, will you?

848
00:31:30,523 --> 00:31:32,225
- Enjoy all this, pal.

849
00:31:32,225 --> 00:31:33,492
Because it's just
gonna be a sweet memory

850
00:31:33,492 --> 00:31:35,362
in your eight by six
box with no shadows.

851
00:31:35,362 --> 00:31:36,595
- You're in the next room.

852
00:31:36,595 --> 00:31:39,632
Uh, kegger's next
door, I believe.

853
00:31:39,632 --> 00:31:40,567
- It's okay.

854
00:31:40,567 --> 00:31:41,567
All right, ladies and gentlemen.

855
00:31:41,567 --> 00:31:42,468
Just a little misunderstanding.

856
00:31:42,468 --> 00:31:43,670
- [Tom] Don't worry.

857
00:31:43,670 --> 00:31:44,470
Just a Van Patten,
ladies and gentlemen.

858
00:31:44,470 --> 00:31:45,405
All a part of the act.

859
00:31:45,405 --> 00:31:47,007
(chuckling) It's okay.

860
00:31:47,007 --> 00:31:49,275
- Kyle, I want that
young man in jail.

861
00:31:49,275 --> 00:31:50,510
- [Joel] Then kill him.

862
00:31:50,510 --> 00:31:52,212
- Cheers, Mr. Keller.

863
00:31:54,047 --> 00:31:55,848
- [Tom] Ooh, right
on the gerbil.

864
00:31:55,848 --> 00:31:57,350
- Oh, indoor-outdoor,
this is the best carpet

865
00:31:57,350 --> 00:32:00,185
I've ever been thrown out on.

866
00:32:00,185 --> 00:32:01,353
- I got thrown out.

867
00:32:01,353 --> 00:32:02,288
- I figured.

868
00:32:04,557 --> 00:32:06,392
- [Joel] Uh, I shop here
for my disco shirts.

869
00:32:06,392 --> 00:32:08,527
- Even Rocky had to
take a couple of lessons

870
00:32:08,527 --> 00:32:10,863
before he went back in the
ring with Clubber Lang.

871
00:32:10,863 --> 00:32:12,265
- [Tom] Club, Clubber Lang?

872
00:32:12,265 --> 00:32:13,598
These are fictional characters
you're talking about.

873
00:32:13,598 --> 00:32:15,167
- Now, if I can't
control your passions,

874
00:32:15,167 --> 00:32:19,072
the least I can do is teach you
enough to stay in one piece.

875
00:32:19,072 --> 00:32:21,373
- I thought you'd never offer.

876
00:32:21,373 --> 00:32:23,375
How do you know about Rocky?

877
00:32:23,375 --> 00:32:25,512
You've been out of the
country for over 30 years.

878
00:32:25,512 --> 00:32:26,745
- I saw him on the airplane.

879
00:32:26,745 --> 00:32:27,847
- [Joel] Yeah, I
tried to walk out.

880
00:32:27,847 --> 00:32:29,048
- Hell of a guy, isn't he?

881
00:32:29,048 --> 00:32:30,683
- [Tom] Ba-boom.

882
00:32:30,683 --> 00:32:31,517
Ah.

883
00:32:32,685 --> 00:32:34,020
- You're kidding with
this outfit, right?

884
00:32:34,020 --> 00:32:35,588
- It's traditional.

885
00:32:35,588 --> 00:32:37,757
We'll ease you into
it. Come at me.

886
00:32:37,757 --> 00:32:38,958
No holds barred.

887
00:32:38,958 --> 00:32:40,460
I'm going to kill you.

888
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:42,662
- [Tom] We're getting into
a whole weird area now.

889
00:32:42,662 --> 00:32:45,332
- You have got to be kidding me.

890
00:32:46,632 --> 00:32:49,268
(Max groaning)

891
00:32:49,268 --> 00:32:51,037
(Tom imitating bones cracking)

892
00:32:51,037 --> 00:32:51,870
- Uncle.

893
00:32:54,707 --> 00:32:55,575
- [Tom] Hm?

894
00:33:01,280 --> 00:33:02,482
- [John] Hone your reflexes

895
00:33:02,482 --> 00:33:04,150
until you react
swifter than thought.

896
00:33:04,150 --> 00:33:05,283
- [Tom] Oh, now you tell me.

897
00:33:05,283 --> 00:33:06,518
- Here, right?

898
00:33:06,518 --> 00:33:08,520
- The center of your
being, inner strength.

899
00:33:08,520 --> 00:33:10,457
- What about getting the outer
strength smacked out of you?

900
00:33:10,457 --> 00:33:13,292
- That's something you should
also be concerned about.

901
00:33:13,292 --> 00:33:14,760
Let's see how you kick.

902
00:33:14,760 --> 00:33:16,028
- [Joel] You know,
black is so slimming

903
00:33:16,028 --> 00:33:17,997
you can't even see
his gut anymore.

904
00:33:17,997 --> 00:33:21,367
- [Tom] Hm, I wonder
what happened?

905
00:33:21,367 --> 00:33:22,602
- Good.

906
00:33:22,602 --> 00:33:24,770
- That was really,
uh, ow! Sonnuva.

907
00:33:24,770 --> 00:33:26,438
- It was still good.

908
00:33:28,875 --> 00:33:30,743
- [Tom] What? Now he's
a, he's a Wallenda?

909
00:33:30,743 --> 00:33:33,045
Yup, yup, he sure is.

910
00:33:33,045 --> 00:33:36,048
- A ninja must have
perfect balance.

911
00:33:40,887 --> 00:33:42,655
- [Joel] Sure. That's
Van Cleef, right?

912
00:33:42,655 --> 00:33:45,725
He can hardly hoist
himself into the van.

913
00:33:45,725 --> 00:33:48,427
- No, this is Lee Van Petit.

914
00:33:48,427 --> 00:33:50,062
(all chuckling)

915
00:33:50,062 --> 00:33:52,065
- [Joel] I don't think so.

916
00:33:52,065 --> 00:33:56,468
- [Tom] Uh, we really
don't need to see that.

917
00:33:56,468 --> 00:33:57,403
Or want to.

918
00:33:59,572 --> 00:34:00,873
David Carradine.

919
00:34:01,773 --> 00:34:04,310
(gentle music)

920
00:34:06,278 --> 00:34:08,513
- And the judges give him a 9.7.

921
00:34:08,513 --> 00:34:09,748
Nice dismount.

922
00:34:09,748 --> 00:34:10,983
- [John] Keep your
eyes on the attack.

923
00:34:10,983 --> 00:34:14,253
- [Joel] Keep your
eye upon the square.

924
00:34:14,253 --> 00:34:16,322
- [Tom] Kaboom.

925
00:34:16,322 --> 00:34:19,192
- [John] From in here, extend.

926
00:34:19,192 --> 00:34:21,427
- Then rake these leaves.

927
00:34:21,427 --> 00:34:25,263
- [John] Expect attack
from any direction.

928
00:34:25,263 --> 00:34:26,265
Concentrate!

929
00:34:28,267 --> 00:34:30,202
- What else you got
in that suitcase?

930
00:34:30,202 --> 00:34:31,403
- [John] When you're ready.

931
00:34:31,403 --> 00:34:35,475
- [Joel] It's a woozle.
His name is Peanut.

932
00:34:35,475 --> 00:34:38,510
- [Tom] Oh, it's Queen
Latifah, of course.

933
00:34:38,510 --> 00:34:40,045
- [Max] I can't hack it.

934
00:34:40,045 --> 00:34:41,547
- Max.

935
00:34:41,547 --> 00:34:43,215
- Yeah, but don't think I'm
walking away from Christensen.

936
00:34:43,215 --> 00:34:46,085
I told him I was gonna
nail him, and I meant it.

937
00:34:46,085 --> 00:34:47,887
Thanks for the lesson.

938
00:34:47,887 --> 00:34:49,255
- That's $45.50 cash.

939
00:34:49,255 --> 00:34:51,323
- You have more tenacity
than I expected,

940
00:34:51,323 --> 00:34:53,058
and speed and courage.

941
00:34:53,058 --> 00:34:55,327
- [Joel] And an agent
who couldn't guarantee
a stunt double.

942
00:34:55,327 --> 00:34:57,397
- It didn't do me
a damn bit of good.

943
00:34:57,397 --> 00:34:59,165
- It showed you can
do more than fight,

944
00:34:59,165 --> 00:35:01,767
and that you're
gonna have to do.

945
00:35:01,767 --> 00:35:03,768
- Now you're beginning
to understand me.

946
00:35:03,768 --> 00:35:05,403
- You have no choice.

947
00:35:05,403 --> 00:35:07,307
You saw Kyle set the
fire at the airport,

948
00:35:07,307 --> 00:35:09,942
you let Christensen
know who you are.

949
00:35:09,942 --> 00:35:11,643
Unless you split town.

950
00:35:11,643 --> 00:35:13,947
- [Tom] All of a sudden it's
a "Barnaby Jones" wrap-up now.

951
00:35:13,947 --> 00:35:17,517
- Fat chance. We'll
have to deal with this.

952
00:35:18,417 --> 00:35:19,918
- We?

953
00:35:19,918 --> 00:35:22,053
- I didn't like what
happened last night.

954
00:35:22,053 --> 00:35:23,055
I didn't like that at all.

955
00:35:23,055 --> 00:35:24,757
- [Tom] It had no texture.

956
00:35:24,757 --> 00:35:25,925
- Maybe the sheriff
would like a visit

957
00:35:25,925 --> 00:35:27,593
from a real, live ninja.

958
00:35:27,593 --> 00:35:29,295
- That could be arranged.

959
00:35:29,295 --> 00:35:31,097
Soon as I get my breath back.

960
00:35:31,097 --> 00:35:34,067
- And some breath mints,
if you don't mind.

961
00:35:34,067 --> 00:35:35,267
- What is it?

962
00:35:35,267 --> 00:35:36,402
- [Joel] Got my breath
back. Feels great.

963
00:35:36,402 --> 00:35:37,570
- A presence.

964
00:35:37,570 --> 00:35:39,405
Let's make that visit.

965
00:35:41,140 --> 00:35:43,575
- [Joel] He is one
spooky mamajama.

966
00:35:43,575 --> 00:35:45,545
(ominous music)

967
00:35:45,545 --> 00:35:48,982
- Than man with the
chainmail face, next.

968
00:35:50,550 --> 00:35:55,287
- [Joel] I was working the day
watch out of Illinois, U.S.A.

969
00:35:55,287 --> 00:35:58,590
♪ You can throw your star at
the man who drives the car ♪

970
00:35:58,590 --> 00:35:59,658
Woo-hoo, woo.

971
00:36:05,230 --> 00:36:07,700
- [Joel] Saw that coming.

972
00:36:07,700 --> 00:36:09,202
Can I have a ride?

973
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:13,072
Does that bug you?

974
00:36:13,072 --> 00:36:14,373
Does that bug you?

975
00:36:14,373 --> 00:36:16,042
- I hate magic acts.

976
00:36:17,777 --> 00:36:21,447
- [Tom] Aw, cripes, and
I'm all out of cars!

977
00:36:24,783 --> 00:36:28,353
(Tom beatboxing)

978
00:36:28,353 --> 00:36:30,488
♪ Wonder Woman ♪

979
00:36:30,488 --> 00:36:33,125
♪ Lyle Waggoner ♪

980
00:36:36,095 --> 00:36:38,097
- [Tom] Ooh, thumbcuffs.

981
00:36:40,700 --> 00:36:42,668
- Who was with you last night
when you torched the airport?

982
00:36:42,668 --> 00:36:43,668
- I dunno what you're---

983
00:36:43,668 --> 00:36:44,570
- Name 'em.

984
00:36:46,938 --> 00:36:48,173
Name 'em.

985
00:36:48,173 --> 00:36:50,108
- [Joel] Phrase in the
form of a question.

986
00:36:50,108 --> 00:36:53,112
- Rosetti, Palmer,
Johnson, Donahue.

987
00:36:54,480 --> 00:36:55,313
- Who are they?

988
00:36:55,313 --> 00:36:56,248
- [Tom] The new Monkees.

989
00:36:56,248 --> 00:36:57,048
- [Kyle] Police reserves.

990
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:57,983
- [Tom] Oh.

991
00:36:59,418 --> 00:37:00,820
- [Max] Every word patched
through to the DA's office.

992
00:37:00,820 --> 00:37:01,720
They'll be by directly.

993
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:03,990
Now where's Christensen?

994
00:37:03,990 --> 00:37:04,923
- Kid--

995
00:37:04,923 --> 00:37:06,092
- I can get mean and nasty.

996
00:37:06,092 --> 00:37:07,760
My friend behind you, you know,

997
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:10,028
the one dressed in black
with the samurai sword?

998
00:37:10,028 --> 00:37:11,130
- Louise Nevelson?

999
00:37:11,130 --> 00:37:12,498
- You know how those ninjas are,

1000
00:37:12,498 --> 00:37:14,700
always going around
beheading each other.

1001
00:37:14,700 --> 00:37:16,535
Barbaric, I know.

1002
00:37:16,535 --> 00:37:18,037
To them it's some
kind of ritual.

1003
00:37:18,037 --> 00:37:18,870
- [Tom] Uh-huh.

1004
00:37:18,870 --> 00:37:20,205
- Know what I mean?

1005
00:37:20,205 --> 00:37:21,407
Now where's Christensen?

1006
00:37:21,407 --> 00:37:23,142
- [Tom] Ooh, I'm
sorry! I'll talk now!

1007
00:37:23,142 --> 00:37:24,543
Ooh, am I scared.

1008
00:37:26,245 --> 00:37:29,015
- [Joel] Hey, Phil. How are ya?

1009
00:37:29,015 --> 00:37:31,217
- I like a man who
keeps his head.

1010
00:37:31,217 --> 00:37:32,150
Don't you?

1011
00:37:32,150 --> 00:37:33,418
- Haha. Again you got me.

1012
00:37:33,418 --> 00:37:34,487
That is rich.

1013
00:37:35,855 --> 00:37:40,525
- [Tom] Next, on a very
special "Trapper John".

1014
00:37:40,525 --> 00:37:43,862
- [Joel] Rub the
Mercedes for good luck.

1015
00:37:49,102 --> 00:37:50,335
- There's a guard in the
lobby at the front desk.

1016
00:37:50,335 --> 00:37:52,270
A lot of monitors
and security guards

1017
00:37:52,270 --> 00:37:53,572
at every floor.
- Well, shut up then!

1018
00:37:53,572 --> 00:37:54,673
- Boss is on the top floor.

1019
00:37:54,673 --> 00:37:55,875
How do we get up there?

1020
00:37:55,875 --> 00:37:58,010
- I would suggest
you use the elevator.

1021
00:37:58,010 --> 00:37:59,078
- How are you
gonna get up there?

1022
00:37:59,078 --> 00:38:00,578
- [John] I'll walk up.

1023
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:01,847
- [Tom] Ew, what did you eat?

1024
00:38:01,847 --> 00:38:02,915
- Stairs?

1025
00:38:02,915 --> 00:38:04,150
- The building.

1026
00:38:06,818 --> 00:38:08,787
- [Max] Sorry I asked.

1027
00:38:08,787 --> 00:38:11,690
(dramatic music)

1028
00:38:11,690 --> 00:38:13,958
- [Joel] Hi, I'm here
to kill Mr. Christensen?

1029
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:15,360
- Oh, go right up,
Mr. Van Patten.

1030
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:19,032
- Max Keller to see
Mr. Christensen.

1031
00:38:19,032 --> 00:38:20,833
- [Tom] Oh, sorry.

1032
00:38:20,833 --> 00:38:22,602
You had a little mustard
down there from lunch.

1033
00:38:22,602 --> 00:38:27,072
- You shoulda gone down
like a sack of flour.

1034
00:38:27,072 --> 00:38:30,375
Sometimes an old-fashioned
right hand cross comes in handy.

1035
00:38:30,375 --> 00:38:34,013
- [Joel] It's a
paperweight and it's a gun.

1036
00:38:34,013 --> 00:38:36,782
(all beatboxing)

1037
00:38:38,217 --> 00:38:42,287
- Clu Gulager is that
character I can't think of.

1038
00:38:43,355 --> 00:38:47,192
- [Joel] "Master Ninja"?
I hate that show.

1039
00:38:47,192 --> 00:38:49,795
- Hey, what're you doing there?

1040
00:38:51,230 --> 00:38:52,765
- [Tom] Well, like I say,
always keeps a supply

1041
00:38:52,765 --> 00:38:54,433
of pegboard hooks
in your pocket.

1042
00:38:54,433 --> 00:38:55,968
You never know when
they'll come in handy.

1043
00:38:55,968 --> 00:38:57,437
- Jacks master.

1044
00:38:57,437 --> 00:38:58,837
- [Tom] In color.

1045
00:39:02,975 --> 00:39:05,510
(Tom beatboxing)

1046
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:06,878
- [Tom] Master Ninja.

1047
00:39:06,878 --> 00:39:09,048
- Aw, nuts. That's my car.

1048
00:39:10,015 --> 00:39:12,518
- [Tom] M-m-m-m-master Ninja.

1049
00:39:17,055 --> 00:39:19,625
(upbeat music)

1050
00:39:23,295 --> 00:39:25,463
- [Joel] Cover your shame.

1051
00:39:29,802 --> 00:39:32,137
[Tom] Ron Cey, ninja doctor.

1052
00:39:33,105 --> 00:39:34,907
(Joel gasping)

1053
00:39:34,907 --> 00:39:36,975
(Tom humming to
background music)

1054
00:39:36,975 --> 00:39:37,810
- Paris!

1055
00:39:39,043 --> 00:39:40,980
- That old man can
take care of himself.

1056
00:39:40,980 --> 00:39:41,813
- Huh?

1057
00:39:44,048 --> 00:39:45,017
Hey, you don't suppose that guy

1058
00:39:45,017 --> 00:39:47,218
was supposed to be that guy?

1059
00:39:47,218 --> 00:39:48,853
And Queen Latifah!

1060
00:39:48,853 --> 00:39:50,588
- [Tom] No way.

1061
00:39:50,588 --> 00:39:53,958
- [Joel] Well, whoever he
is, his nose is whistling.

1062
00:39:53,958 --> 00:39:55,493
- And he was that
guy? Unbelievable!

1063
00:39:55,493 --> 00:39:56,828
He was in every
scene in the movie!

1064
00:39:56,828 --> 00:39:58,030
He was Demi Moore!

1065
00:39:58,030 --> 00:39:59,265
He was that gerbil! He was--

1066
00:39:59,265 --> 00:40:02,067
- [Tom] Crow, Crow,
easy, easy, buddy.

1067
00:40:02,968 --> 00:40:05,637
(all whistling)

1068
00:40:07,973 --> 00:40:10,075
And just grab the 7-iron.

1069
00:40:11,277 --> 00:40:13,645
- [Joel] Clarence
the cross-eyed ninja.

1070
00:40:13,645 --> 00:40:15,647
- [Tom] He who removeth
the sword from its sheath

1071
00:40:15,647 --> 00:40:19,952
shall be the rightwiseborn
king of England.

1072
00:40:19,952 --> 00:40:22,922
- [Joel] Conhuge
Co. welcomes you.

1073
00:40:22,922 --> 00:40:25,590
(all whistling)

1074
00:40:27,258 --> 00:40:28,460
- Hey, Lee.

1075
00:40:28,460 --> 00:40:29,628
You wanna check those
bags at the door?

1076
00:40:29,628 --> 00:40:31,330
(all chuckling)

1077
00:40:31,330 --> 00:40:32,330
- [Tom] Woo.

1078
00:40:35,233 --> 00:40:39,638
- I think I'll check my
credit rating while I'm here.

1079
00:40:43,575 --> 00:40:45,610
(whistling)

1080
00:40:45,610 --> 00:40:47,713
- [Joel] Hi, I'm Bonnie,
your Conhuge Co. operator.

1081
00:40:47,713 --> 00:40:51,517
Oh, back to work. (chuckling)

1082
00:40:53,652 --> 00:40:57,490
- [Tom] The ninja creeps
in on little cat feet.

1083
00:41:00,558 --> 00:41:01,660
- Am I in the right movie?

1084
00:41:01,660 --> 00:41:04,230
Hey, Lee, come over here a sec.

1085
00:41:05,865 --> 00:41:06,798
- [Tom] Wait.

1086
00:41:06,798 --> 00:41:08,967
Whose theme music is that?

1087
00:41:08,967 --> 00:41:12,470
- [Joel] Can he sneeze
through that thing?

1088
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:14,707
He's wearing a Joe Namath
netted slingshot brief

1089
00:41:14,707 --> 00:41:15,707
on his face.

1090
00:41:17,108 --> 00:41:18,810
- Yeah, meanwhile Timothy's
having a Nam flashback.

1091
00:41:18,810 --> 00:41:19,912
- [Joel] Ooh.

1092
00:41:21,413 --> 00:41:23,415
- [Tom] And over here
of the 30th floor

1093
00:41:23,415 --> 00:41:26,818
of the Ernest and Julio
Gallo wine cellar.

1094
00:41:26,818 --> 00:41:28,087
- [Max] Christensen.

1095
00:41:28,087 --> 00:41:29,255
(gun firing)
(glass breaking)

1096
00:41:29,255 --> 00:41:31,057
- Who is it!?

1097
00:41:31,057 --> 00:41:33,325
- Helicopter's a late, huh?

1098
00:41:34,727 --> 00:41:35,560
Too bad.

1099
00:41:36,862 --> 00:41:38,263
Your lawyer, Mr.
Havilland and Sheriff Kyle

1100
00:41:38,263 --> 00:41:39,465
are both under arrest.

1101
00:41:39,465 --> 00:41:40,698
- [Joel] Oh, they are?

1102
00:41:40,698 --> 00:41:41,833
I, I have no idea
what's going on.

1103
00:41:41,833 --> 00:41:43,735
- [Max] But of
course you know that.

1104
00:41:43,735 --> 00:41:46,505
That's why you're
leaving in such a hurry.

1105
00:41:46,505 --> 00:41:50,508
- [Tom] His office
looks like a Chi Chi's.

1106
00:41:50,508 --> 00:41:53,512
- Hey, bring me those nachos!

1107
00:41:53,512 --> 00:41:54,480
- [Max] Sometimes
things just don't

1108
00:41:54,480 --> 00:41:56,015
work out the way you planned.

1109
00:41:56,015 --> 00:41:57,617
- [Tom] Oh, and on top of it
all, he's a ventriloquist.

1110
00:41:57,617 --> 00:42:01,187
- I'm glad we had this chance
to meet again, Mr. Keller.

1111
00:42:01,187 --> 00:42:02,487
Otherwise your grandstand
play last night

1112
00:42:02,487 --> 00:42:04,257
wouldn't mean a thing, would it?

1113
00:42:04,257 --> 00:42:05,992
- [Joel] 'Cause it
ain't got no swing.

1114
00:42:05,992 --> 00:42:08,593
- [Tom] And your friends are
the only creeps in this place.

1115
00:42:08,593 --> 00:42:10,862
- It's better late than never.

1116
00:42:10,862 --> 00:42:13,032
- [Max] Just one question.

1117
00:42:15,033 --> 00:42:16,902
- [Tom] Can I use
your fax machine?

1118
00:42:16,902 --> 00:42:18,537
- And what would that be?

1119
00:42:18,537 --> 00:42:20,805
- [Max] How do you plan
on getting up on the roof?

1120
00:42:20,805 --> 00:42:22,073
- [Tom] Hmm.

1121
00:42:22,073 --> 00:42:24,477
- You really think you
can stop me, Keller?

1122
00:42:24,477 --> 00:42:26,078
- [Max] Just keep talking, pal.

1123
00:42:26,078 --> 00:42:27,947
(gun firing)

1124
00:42:27,947 --> 00:42:30,382
- Oh, it's a
ventriloquist pistol.

1125
00:42:30,382 --> 00:42:35,387
- [Tom] (chuckling) Say
hello to folks, Remington.

1126
00:42:37,657 --> 00:42:40,292
- I got a bad feeling about
that knickknack shelf.

1127
00:42:40,292 --> 00:42:42,460
- [Joel] Uh-huh. I see it.

1128
00:42:46,398 --> 00:42:47,700
- [Tom] Kids, what was that?

1129
00:42:47,700 --> 00:42:50,902
- [Joel and Crow] Nothing, mom.

1130
00:42:50,902 --> 00:42:52,337
- [Joel] Good thing he
studied with that ninja

1131
00:42:52,337 --> 00:42:54,707
for those 10 minutes.

1132
00:42:54,707 --> 00:42:56,175
- Check out, Jack.

1133
00:42:57,442 --> 00:42:59,077
- [Tom] Wow, this
movie is clueless.

1134
00:42:59,077 --> 00:43:00,312
Woohoo!

1135
00:43:00,312 --> 00:43:02,948
- Yeah, 'cause there's, he died.

1136
00:43:05,117 --> 00:43:07,318
Meanwhile in the other
incomprehensible plot,

1137
00:43:07,318 --> 00:43:09,220
Queen Latifah takes a--

1138
00:43:10,322 --> 00:43:12,557
(Tom humming background music)

1139
00:43:12,557 --> 00:43:13,992
- [John] I've been
expecting you.

1140
00:43:13,992 --> 00:43:17,395
- [Ninja] A ninja does
not betray his destiny.

1141
00:43:17,395 --> 00:43:18,497
You will die.

1142
00:43:19,698 --> 00:43:20,765
- [Tom] Okay, fine.
Just wait a second.

1143
00:43:20,765 --> 00:43:23,435
Let me park the tape drive here.

1144
00:43:26,272 --> 00:43:29,342
- [Joel] You didn't pay
for your leather mug!

1145
00:43:29,342 --> 00:43:33,278
(Tom imitating arrow twanging)

1146
00:43:35,647 --> 00:43:36,882
- Why didn't he just kill him

1147
00:43:36,882 --> 00:43:38,550
when he was watching
him from the tree?

1148
00:43:38,550 --> 00:43:42,220
- [Joel] Those things
are $4.50 apiece.

1149
00:43:42,220 --> 00:43:43,422
- [Tom] (chuckling) Okay.

1150
00:43:43,422 --> 00:43:45,992
One more, and then
to bed for you.

1151
00:43:49,828 --> 00:43:51,863
- I'll take him.

1152
00:43:51,863 --> 00:43:54,633
(ninja shouting)

1153
00:43:58,903 --> 00:44:00,972
- Okay, you take him now.

1154
00:44:08,247 --> 00:44:09,582
- [Joel] Huzzah.

1155
00:44:12,117 --> 00:44:13,118
- [Tom] Oof.

1156
00:44:16,522 --> 00:44:18,123
Okay, okay, knock it off.

1157
00:44:18,123 --> 00:44:21,293
You're getting
obnoxious about it now.

1158
00:44:22,227 --> 00:44:24,897
(both shouting)

1159
00:44:30,768 --> 00:44:32,037
- [Joel] You know,
Doris is gonna be irked

1160
00:44:32,037 --> 00:44:33,938
if she sees this
mess in the morning.

1161
00:44:33,938 --> 00:44:34,940
- [Tom] Yup.

1162
00:44:38,577 --> 00:44:42,013
Ah, there go the
financials for December.

1163
00:44:44,950 --> 00:44:46,485
- I, I'll take him.

1164
00:44:49,555 --> 00:44:51,057
- [Tom] Make 'em laugh!

1165
00:44:51,057 --> 00:44:52,290
Make 'em laugh!

1166
00:45:01,067 --> 00:45:02,902
- [Joel] The nunchuks, Luke.

1167
00:45:02,902 --> 00:45:04,335
Use the nunchuks.

1168
00:45:05,737 --> 00:45:08,073
- [Tom] Trust your feelings.

1169
00:45:11,910 --> 00:45:12,745
- Oh, a leather punch. Cool.

1170
00:45:12,745 --> 00:45:15,413
(both shouting)

1171
00:45:19,652 --> 00:45:20,652
- [Tom] Ooh.

1172
00:45:26,258 --> 00:45:29,327
- [Joel] That thing's
got everything.

1173
00:45:30,695 --> 00:45:32,430
- [Tom] A lot of yelling.

1174
00:45:32,430 --> 00:45:37,002
- Oh, now you've ruined the
whole ambience of the room.

1175
00:45:40,372 --> 00:45:42,875
- [Tom] I'll take it
from here. I'll clean up.

1176
00:45:42,875 --> 00:45:44,308
- [Ninja] You are a ninja.

1177
00:45:44,308 --> 00:45:48,813
Kill your enemy as you've
always done, kyojin.

1178
00:45:48,813 --> 00:45:50,048
- What? A Kirin?

1179
00:45:50,048 --> 00:45:51,117
Ah, yeah. I could
go for a Kirin.

1180
00:45:51,117 --> 00:45:52,450
- [John] Never again.

1181
00:45:52,450 --> 00:45:54,252
- [Joel] No more
raspberry commies.

1182
00:45:54,252 --> 00:45:56,155
- [Ninja] There will
be another time.

1183
00:45:56,155 --> 00:45:58,457
They will be coming for you.

1184
00:45:59,692 --> 00:46:01,527
- If you could just
take this off my chest,

1185
00:46:01,527 --> 00:46:04,597
and move it to the
side, it would be most--

1186
00:46:04,597 --> 00:46:06,030
- [John] I'll be waiting.

1187
00:46:06,030 --> 00:46:09,367
- [Joel] In all the
old familiar places.

1188
00:46:10,235 --> 00:46:11,170
(all groaning)

1189
00:46:11,170 --> 00:46:14,038
- [Tom] I always do that.

1190
00:46:14,038 --> 00:46:16,142
- Don't turn your
back on that guy.

1191
00:46:16,142 --> 00:46:19,845
- You see what he
did to me last time?

1192
00:46:19,845 --> 00:46:21,580
- He won't fight again tonight.

1193
00:46:21,580 --> 00:46:22,413
I'm certain.

1194
00:46:22,413 --> 00:46:23,615
An artery was severed.

1195
00:46:23,615 --> 00:46:24,583
- [Tom] Boy, and he's
not even bleeding.

1196
00:46:24,583 --> 00:46:25,517
- Who is he?

1197
00:46:25,517 --> 00:46:27,987
- Okasa, now a ninja master.

1198
00:46:27,987 --> 00:46:30,022
Was one of my students.

1199
00:46:30,022 --> 00:46:31,690
- Sent to kill you.

1200
00:46:31,690 --> 00:46:32,825
What ancient little
gadget did you use

1201
00:46:32,825 --> 00:46:34,793
to sever Okasa's artery?

1202
00:46:34,793 --> 00:46:36,395
- My fingers.

1203
00:46:36,395 --> 00:46:37,930
- [Joel] Sticky fingers.

1204
00:46:37,930 --> 00:46:39,263
- Sorry I asked.

1205
00:46:41,500 --> 00:46:44,870
- [Tom] Not designed as
a real sword, only a toy.

1206
00:46:44,870 --> 00:46:45,703
Darn!

1207
00:46:47,405 --> 00:46:48,240
- Mendoza!

1208
00:46:50,675 --> 00:46:51,843
- [Joel] Epilogue.

1209
00:46:51,843 --> 00:46:53,745
- [Max] Holly knows
your daughter.

1210
00:46:53,745 --> 00:46:55,013
She's in Atlanta.

1211
00:46:55,013 --> 00:46:56,215
- [John] Is she all right?

1212
00:46:56,215 --> 00:46:57,515
- Find that out
when you get there.

1213
00:46:57,515 --> 00:47:00,252
I can take you that far.

1214
00:47:00,252 --> 00:47:01,487
- [Tom] Hm.

1215
00:47:01,487 --> 00:47:03,655
I hope she's into
big-ass medallions.

1216
00:47:03,655 --> 00:47:04,790
- It's pretty.

1217
00:47:06,258 --> 00:47:07,625
- Symbol of my household.
- I got it from Bob Vila.

1218
00:47:07,625 --> 00:47:09,728
- It's what Okasa wanted.

1219
00:47:09,728 --> 00:47:11,095
- I don't get it.

1220
00:47:11,095 --> 00:47:12,130
- For another man to possess it

1221
00:47:12,130 --> 00:47:14,900
would mean I was
no longer alive.

1222
00:47:16,067 --> 00:47:18,170
- You guys got your
own set of rules.

1223
00:47:18,170 --> 00:47:19,705
No one else can play, huh?

1224
00:47:19,705 --> 00:47:21,273
- [Joel] Yeah, and I'm
always the banker, punk.

1225
00:47:21,273 --> 00:47:24,008
- I was taught the secrets
of the ninjas for a purpose.

1226
00:47:24,008 --> 00:47:25,510
So that I might
pass them on the way

1227
00:47:25,510 --> 00:47:27,512
my master passed them on to me.

1228
00:47:27,512 --> 00:47:30,815
- And I end up with a
has-been from "White Shadow".

1229
00:47:30,815 --> 00:47:34,687
- What good is a ninja
teacher without a student?

1230
00:47:34,687 --> 00:47:36,988
- [Tom] Well, those
who can't ninja, teach.

1231
00:47:36,988 --> 00:47:39,157
(mellow music)

1232
00:47:39,157 --> 00:47:41,158
- [Joel] Hey, here
comes Betty Jo.

1233
00:47:41,158 --> 00:47:42,193
Hi!

1234
00:47:42,193 --> 00:47:43,962
- [Tom] Hi, Betty Jo.

1235
00:47:45,497 --> 00:47:48,667
- I've met people
way cooler than you!

1236
00:47:50,868 --> 00:47:52,170
- [Tom] Let's roll, folks.

1237
00:47:52,170 --> 00:47:54,773
- Say hi to the Brat Pack!

1238
00:47:54,773 --> 00:47:56,508
- Look out for that
thing, what the hell?

1239
00:47:56,508 --> 00:47:57,842
- [Joel] I think
it's over there.

1240
00:47:57,842 --> 00:48:00,278
- You're getting scary again.

1241
00:48:03,382 --> 00:48:05,917
(upbeat music)

1242
00:48:10,822 --> 00:48:12,023
- Yes, yes.

1243
00:48:12,023 --> 00:48:14,125
Found myself in
Japan after the war.

1244
00:48:14,125 --> 00:48:16,428
Boy, talk about tranquil, whew!

1245
00:48:16,428 --> 00:48:17,662
Let me tell ya.

1246
00:48:17,662 --> 00:48:19,097
But anyway, I got
to know some ninjas.

1247
00:48:19,097 --> 00:48:20,332
Hey, they're great guys,

1248
00:48:20,332 --> 00:48:21,767
and they're thick
as flies over there.

1249
00:48:21,767 --> 00:48:24,435
Well, one thing led to
another, and I found myself--

1250
00:48:24,435 --> 00:48:25,903
- Yaa!

1251
00:48:25,903 --> 00:48:27,838
You're impressed at
Occidental Roser.

1252
00:48:27,838 --> 00:48:29,473
Me and my scary theme
music will follow you

1253
00:48:29,473 --> 00:48:31,610
and your plastic katana sword
to the ends of the Earth!

1254
00:48:31,610 --> 00:48:33,312
And then I will-

1255
00:48:33,312 --> 00:48:34,345
(both laughing)

1256
00:48:34,345 --> 00:48:35,980
- Come here!

1257
00:48:35,980 --> 00:48:37,482
You and your cheap,
cheap, Japanese accent!

1258
00:48:37,482 --> 00:48:40,552
- You can tell, you can
tell by my theme music

1259
00:48:40,552 --> 00:48:42,587
that I'm a typical American.

1260
00:48:42,587 --> 00:48:44,422
You wanna see the
way we leave a bar?

1261
00:48:44,422 --> 00:48:45,257
Whoa!

1262
00:48:46,958 --> 00:48:50,962
- The power of my music is
the weakness of my music!

1263
00:48:50,962 --> 00:48:53,898
You with your crummy
Oriental accent!

1264
00:48:53,898 --> 00:48:55,333
Grr.

1265
00:48:55,333 --> 00:48:56,835
- There's nothing like a
good old-fashioned left hook!

1266
00:48:56,835 --> 00:48:57,668
- Ow!

1267
00:48:59,003 --> 00:49:01,673
- Hey, cool it, you guys.

1268
00:49:01,673 --> 00:49:04,242
- Hey, hey, Gypsy, what
are you supposed to be?

1269
00:49:04,242 --> 00:49:05,643
- Gigi.

1270
00:49:05,643 --> 00:49:08,313
- Don't you wanna be Demi Moore?

1271
00:49:09,213 --> 00:49:10,448
- It's show--

1272
00:49:10,448 --> 00:49:11,883
- [Forrester] Don't even
think about it, Frank.

1273
00:49:11,883 --> 00:49:14,152
Send him the movie.

1274
00:49:14,152 --> 00:49:14,987
- Time.

1275
00:49:18,023 --> 00:49:20,325
(Klaxon blaring)
(all shouting)

1276
00:49:20,325 --> 00:49:23,095
- We got movie
sign, it's coming!

1277
00:49:35,107 --> 00:49:38,477
(energetic dance music)

1278
00:49:38,477 --> 00:49:40,312
- Uh, could we see
a menu, please?

1279
00:49:40,312 --> 00:49:41,780
- That's Kelly Pattersen.

1280
00:49:41,780 --> 00:49:43,082
She was the girl standing
next to your daughter.

1281
00:49:43,082 --> 00:49:44,883
- [Joel] Sleep!

1282
00:49:44,883 --> 00:49:46,952
- Her old man runs this place.

1283
00:49:46,952 --> 00:49:48,953
I'll try and catch
her after this dance.

1284
00:49:48,953 --> 00:49:50,055
We don't wanna
integrate you too fast

1285
00:49:50,055 --> 00:49:51,423
into modern-day society.

1286
00:49:51,423 --> 00:49:52,723
- [Tom] Good point.

1287
00:49:52,723 --> 00:49:54,092
- All right. You go
talk the pretty girl.

1288
00:49:54,092 --> 00:49:56,193
I'll talk to her father.

1289
00:49:56,193 --> 00:49:57,495
- What a pal.

1290
00:49:57,495 --> 00:49:58,797
- Any time.

1291
00:49:58,797 --> 00:50:00,198
- I love the way they banter.

1292
00:50:00,198 --> 00:50:02,067
Such chemistry!

1293
00:50:02,067 --> 00:50:03,435
- [Tom] Uh, Miss,
could we please

1294
00:50:03,435 --> 00:50:05,770
get some bread or something?

1295
00:50:10,642 --> 00:50:14,145
- She owes me $5. (sniffling)

1296
00:50:14,145 --> 00:50:17,382
♪ Staying a guy, staying a guy ♪

1297
00:50:17,382 --> 00:50:18,583
Jack Perkins?

1298
00:50:18,583 --> 00:50:20,318
- No!
- Oh, yeah.

1299
00:50:20,318 --> 00:50:21,218
- Jack, no!

1300
00:50:23,255 --> 00:50:25,257
- [Tom] Oh my.

1301
00:50:25,257 --> 00:50:26,658
- [Joel] Hey, what
happened to Demi Moore?

1302
00:50:26,658 --> 00:50:27,992
This is getting weird.

1303
00:50:27,992 --> 00:50:28,827
- Oh yeah.

1304
00:50:31,062 --> 00:50:32,397
- [Tom] Oh, swing it, Lee.

1305
00:50:32,397 --> 00:50:34,065
Woo, look at him go.

1306
00:50:38,270 --> 00:50:39,237
Oh my god.

1307
00:50:39,237 --> 00:50:40,972
What happened to her other leg?

1308
00:50:40,972 --> 00:50:42,373
Oh.
- There it is.

1309
00:50:42,373 --> 00:50:45,210
(audience cheering)

1310
00:50:45,210 --> 00:50:47,312
- [Tom] Woo. Woo.

1311
00:50:47,312 --> 00:50:49,748
- Mrs. Ironside in color.

1312
00:50:49,748 --> 00:50:52,117
(whistling)

1313
00:50:52,117 --> 00:50:53,818
- She's something, isn't she?

1314
00:50:53,818 --> 00:50:55,987
- A true spirit,
permeated with joy.

1315
00:50:55,987 --> 00:50:57,422
And she moves great.

1316
00:50:57,422 --> 00:50:58,890
- You betcha.

1317
00:50:58,890 --> 00:51:01,358
- [Joel] We're bald
and we're bonding.

1318
00:51:01,358 --> 00:51:02,693
- Where's Jill?

1319
00:51:02,693 --> 00:51:03,995
- She's in the kitchen.

1320
00:51:03,995 --> 00:51:06,498
- She's watching old
movies, Mr. Pattersen.

1321
00:51:06,498 --> 00:51:07,565
- Mr. Pattersen?

1322
00:51:07,565 --> 00:51:10,035
- I'll be right with you.

1323
00:51:10,035 --> 00:51:12,170
- [Tom] He's a queer duck, eh?

1324
00:51:12,170 --> 00:51:15,273
(audience cheering)

1325
00:51:15,273 --> 00:51:17,275
- [Tom] Woo. Woo. Woo.

1326
00:51:17,275 --> 00:51:21,547
- I, uh, hate to burst your
bubble, but she stinks.

1327
00:51:22,580 --> 00:51:24,315
- No one's allowed backstage.

1328
00:51:24,315 --> 00:51:25,983
- [Joel] It's Alan Thicke!

1329
00:51:25,983 --> 00:51:26,785
- [Tom] Oh.

1330
00:51:26,785 --> 00:51:28,153
- Oh, uh, Kim.

1331
00:51:28,153 --> 00:51:29,988
- Just enjoy the show.

1332
00:51:32,290 --> 00:51:34,793
- Hi, we're here
to buy everything.

1333
00:51:34,793 --> 00:51:38,397
- [Joel] Fusion jazz
is for all cultures.

1334
00:51:38,397 --> 00:51:40,898
(Tom humming)

1335
00:51:42,367 --> 00:51:44,102
- [Tom] Now that's one way
to get service, I suppose.

1336
00:51:44,102 --> 00:51:45,803
- [Max] Perhaps you can help us.

1337
00:51:45,803 --> 00:51:49,607
- [Joel] Candy-coated
popcorn peanuts and a prize.

1338
00:51:49,607 --> 00:51:51,408
- We've come to
see Mr. Pattersen.

1339
00:51:51,408 --> 00:51:53,978
- In the office over there.

1340
00:51:53,978 --> 00:51:55,013
- Thank you so much.

1341
00:51:55,013 --> 00:51:57,048
- [Tom] Oh no, thank you.

1342
00:52:00,085 --> 00:52:03,488
- Looks like Clarence
Thomas's wife.

1343
00:52:03,488 --> 00:52:04,755
- [Tom] It does.

1344
00:52:06,992 --> 00:52:08,025
Oh, Lee, don't worry.

1345
00:52:08,025 --> 00:52:08,960
She's used to it.

1346
00:52:08,960 --> 00:52:12,063
The Kennedys come here a lot.

1347
00:52:12,063 --> 00:52:14,265
- You'd think with
all the roughnecks

1348
00:52:14,265 --> 00:52:17,235
we get in this place
I'd be used to it.

1349
00:52:17,235 --> 00:52:18,770
- You were right to be afraid.

1350
00:52:18,770 --> 00:52:21,205
- [Joel] Be very afraid.

1351
00:52:21,205 --> 00:52:22,940
- [Tom] My, but you
area sensitive male.

1352
00:52:22,940 --> 00:52:23,775
See you.

1353
00:52:25,577 --> 00:52:28,313
- Oh, it's the other
side of the mountain.

1354
00:52:28,313 --> 00:52:29,915
- [Charlie] What
are you doing, Jill?

1355
00:52:29,915 --> 00:52:31,415
- [Jill] I'm watching you
and Mother dance the waltz

1356
00:52:31,415 --> 00:52:33,352
from "Lady Be Good".

1357
00:52:33,352 --> 00:52:35,420
- Down in front, old man!

1358
00:52:37,022 --> 00:52:39,723
- [Tom] Ah, you know, Fred
Astaire and Ginger Rogers.

1359
00:52:39,723 --> 00:52:41,025
Love them.
- Look at that lift.

1360
00:52:41,025 --> 00:52:42,027
Look at the way you moved.

1361
00:52:42,027 --> 00:52:43,195
You were so graceful.

1362
00:52:43,195 --> 00:52:44,662
- [Joel] Yet so effeminate.

1363
00:52:44,662 --> 00:52:46,497
- I'll just bet you
had Mr. Astaire shaking

1364
00:52:46,497 --> 00:52:48,165
in his dancing pumps.

1365
00:52:48,165 --> 00:52:49,833
- I was his dresser actually.

1366
00:52:49,833 --> 00:52:51,235
- I don't think he
was shaking too hard.

1367
00:52:51,235 --> 00:52:52,570
- You think it's kind
of sicko for the leader

1368
00:52:52,570 --> 00:52:54,805
of a wheelchair brigade
to get such a charge

1369
00:52:54,805 --> 00:52:56,608
out of watching
other people dance?

1370
00:52:56,608 --> 00:52:58,108
- Yes, actually.

1371
00:52:58,108 --> 00:52:59,377
- [Jill] I don't mean
the way my sister dances.

1372
00:52:59,377 --> 00:53:00,612
That's not dancing.

1373
00:53:00,612 --> 00:53:02,847
- It's typing.
- That's aerobics.

1374
00:53:02,847 --> 00:53:05,283
Now what you did was dancing.

1375
00:53:05,283 --> 00:53:07,418
Bet you could still do it, too.

1376
00:53:07,418 --> 00:53:08,353
If you really wanted to.

1377
00:53:08,353 --> 00:53:09,687
- [Joel] Maybe if I had a hip.

1378
00:53:09,687 --> 00:53:12,157
- Or if he was hip.
- You're right, dad.

1379
00:53:12,157 --> 00:53:15,160
With some hot towels on my
legs at half hourly intervals,

1380
00:53:15,160 --> 00:53:16,995
couple of FDR canes.
- Oh, yes.

1381
00:53:16,995 --> 00:53:18,430
Oh, yeah.

1382
00:53:18,430 --> 00:53:19,697
- I might be able to
manage a couple of steps.

1383
00:53:19,697 --> 00:53:23,302
- A cane didn't hurt
Mr. Astaire's career.

1384
00:53:23,302 --> 00:53:24,468
- [Joel] Oh, bite me.

1385
00:53:24,468 --> 00:53:26,503
- Don't you just
hate dealing with it?

1386
00:53:26,503 --> 00:53:27,972
An ex-hoofer with two daughters.

1387
00:53:27,972 --> 00:53:29,473
- [Tom] Hooker? Oh, hoofer.

1388
00:53:29,473 --> 00:53:31,342
- One wheels, the
other cartwheels.

1389
00:53:31,342 --> 00:53:35,947
- One is shy and retiring,
and, uh, one has a smart mouth.

1390
00:53:35,947 --> 00:53:36,915
- [Tom] Ooh, touche.

1391
00:53:36,915 --> 00:53:38,850
- My sister, shy and retiring?

1392
00:53:38,850 --> 00:53:40,885
The decade's answer
to Isadora Duncan?

1393
00:53:40,885 --> 00:53:43,888
- [Joel] What?
She wears scarves?

1394
00:53:43,888 --> 00:53:45,590
- That's angry Jill.

1395
00:53:45,590 --> 00:53:47,225
- Sorry. I'm bitter.

1396
00:53:47,225 --> 00:53:48,893
- I wonder what she calls me.

1397
00:53:48,893 --> 00:53:49,827
- Gimp?

1398
00:53:49,827 --> 00:53:51,095
- [Joel] Oh, that's mean.

1399
00:53:51,095 --> 00:53:52,530
- Isn't that what
you call yourself?

1400
00:53:52,530 --> 00:53:53,465
- Hey, now. Wait a minute.

1401
00:53:53,465 --> 00:53:54,898
I took two steps yesterday.

1402
00:53:54,898 --> 00:53:55,967
- [Tom] Time to go, honey.

1403
00:53:55,967 --> 00:53:56,802
- I know.

1404
00:53:56,802 --> 00:53:57,735
- Oh.

1405
00:53:57,735 --> 00:53:59,170
This is my favorite part.

1406
00:53:59,170 --> 00:54:01,472
This is your audition
for the dancing pirate.

1407
00:54:01,472 --> 00:54:02,840
This, this is a blast.

1408
00:54:02,840 --> 00:54:05,477
- You were really gadding it up.

1409
00:54:07,012 --> 00:54:10,482
- [Joel] We'd like to
buy her wheelchair.

1410
00:54:10,482 --> 00:54:12,450
- Mr. Pattersen,
how good to meet you

1411
00:54:12,450 --> 00:54:14,953
in person after all
those phone calls.

1412
00:54:14,953 --> 00:54:18,423
I'm Jonathan Chan,
and this is Mr. Lika.

1413
00:54:18,423 --> 00:54:20,725
- Uh, are you related
to Mr. Phlegm?

1414
00:54:20,725 --> 00:54:22,360
- Would you excuse
us, young lady?

1415
00:54:22,360 --> 00:54:25,997
Your father and I have some
important business to discuss.

1416
00:54:25,997 --> 00:54:27,398
- In a pig's eye.

1417
00:54:27,398 --> 00:54:28,633
- Jill, come on.

1418
00:54:28,633 --> 00:54:30,968
- [Tom] One talks
of pigs, one sweats.

1419
00:54:30,968 --> 00:54:32,170
- Watch your feet, gentlemen.

1420
00:54:32,170 --> 00:54:35,140
I'm lethal with this
thing. You mind?

1421
00:54:37,675 --> 00:54:38,977
- [Tom] Ooh, my foot.

1422
00:54:38,977 --> 00:54:40,578
Oof.

1423
00:54:40,578 --> 00:54:42,680
- So let's talk business.

1424
00:54:44,182 --> 00:54:45,250
- There's a little
trouble up front.

1425
00:54:45,250 --> 00:54:46,450
- Big China.

1426
00:54:46,450 --> 00:54:47,952
- [Max] While Attila
the Hun was distracted,

1427
00:54:47,952 --> 00:54:49,653
I saw my chance
to get backstage.

1428
00:54:49,653 --> 00:54:51,455
This was gonna be easy.

1429
00:54:51,455 --> 00:54:53,290
- [Joel] At first.

1430
00:54:53,290 --> 00:54:54,958
- [Tom] Oops.

1431
00:54:54,958 --> 00:54:57,862
(women chattering)

1432
00:54:59,030 --> 00:55:02,233
- Hey, can I get
a pencil in here?

1433
00:55:02,233 --> 00:55:04,335
Okay, give me the number.

1434
00:55:05,837 --> 00:55:07,238
Okay.

1435
00:55:07,238 --> 00:55:10,308
- Thank god I lost my
peripheral vision in the war.

1436
00:55:10,308 --> 00:55:13,612
- [Tom] Hey, what is this?
"Dream On" all of a sudden?

1437
00:55:13,612 --> 00:55:14,445
- Hey.

1438
00:55:15,580 --> 00:55:16,513
Don't take your
hand from your eyes

1439
00:55:16,513 --> 00:55:17,915
you're gonna walk into the wall.

1440
00:55:17,915 --> 00:55:20,952
- You got a D cup or,
it's decaf. Decaf.

1441
00:55:20,952 --> 00:55:22,187
- You really shouldn't
be back here.

1442
00:55:22,187 --> 00:55:25,057
Our bouncer has a small
personality problem.

1443
00:55:25,057 --> 00:55:26,157
- Who? Attila the Hun?

1444
00:55:26,157 --> 00:55:27,092
We're pals.

1445
00:55:27,992 --> 00:55:30,395
Kelly Pattersen, I'm Max Keller.

1446
00:55:30,395 --> 00:55:31,362
Looking for a girl.

1447
00:55:31,362 --> 00:55:32,897
- [Joel] New or used?

1448
00:55:32,897 --> 00:55:34,165
- If the stars are in the
right places it'd be you.

1449
00:55:34,165 --> 00:55:35,333
The name's Terry.

1450
00:55:35,333 --> 00:55:36,567
You know her?

1451
00:55:36,567 --> 00:55:39,037
- Uh, no dancer
here named Terry.

1452
00:55:39,037 --> 00:55:41,505
Look, we're on a break now,
and I've gotta go meet someone.

1453
00:55:41,505 --> 00:55:43,240
Sorry.
- Yeah, but I--

1454
00:55:43,240 --> 00:55:44,075
- Sorry.

1455
00:55:45,477 --> 00:55:46,878
- Just take a look at
this picture and see if--

1456
00:55:46,878 --> 00:55:48,413
- Is it my breath?

1457
00:55:48,413 --> 00:55:51,182
- [Max] Wasn't as
easy as I thought.

1458
00:55:51,182 --> 00:55:52,117
- [Tom] And it's
time for the bouncer

1459
00:55:52,117 --> 00:55:54,785
to get into his spandex leotard.

1460
00:55:57,822 --> 00:55:58,990
- [Joel] Mwah!

1461
00:56:00,425 --> 00:56:02,793
- Kelly did mention a small
personality problem of yours.

1462
00:56:02,793 --> 00:56:05,730
- [Tom] Yeah, you
hate Van Pattens.

1463
00:56:07,598 --> 00:56:10,368
- It's the Battle of
the Network Has-beens!

1464
00:56:10,368 --> 00:56:11,368
- [Tom] Woo.

1465
00:56:13,270 --> 00:56:14,405
- [Joel] Yeah, that's for
all of the Van Pattens

1466
00:56:14,405 --> 00:56:15,773
you've kicked out of bars.

1467
00:56:15,773 --> 00:56:17,442
- How do you like this, pal?

1468
00:56:17,442 --> 00:56:19,777
Here's a little warning.

1469
00:56:19,777 --> 00:56:22,280
- [Joel] Uh-oh. Seven
years bad acting.

1470
00:56:22,280 --> 00:56:24,048
- Need more practice.

1471
00:56:26,217 --> 00:56:28,285
- I told you eight is enough!

1472
00:56:28,285 --> 00:56:30,922
- [Max] So seven years bad luck.

1473
00:56:32,290 --> 00:56:33,658
Meanwhile, the
master was getting us

1474
00:56:33,658 --> 00:56:35,127
into even more trouble.

1475
00:56:35,127 --> 00:56:38,597
- [Tom] Snapping off car
antennas in the parking lot.

1476
00:56:38,597 --> 00:56:41,565
- [Joel] You ninja
masters blend in so well.

1477
00:56:41,565 --> 00:56:43,033
- [Tom] Especially in discos.

1478
00:56:43,033 --> 00:56:46,838
- Like the roots of a great
oak, we take hold where we can.

1479
00:56:46,838 --> 00:56:50,808
- The only protection I need
is from people like you.

1480
00:56:50,808 --> 00:56:51,810
Now get out.

1481
00:56:52,977 --> 00:56:55,580
- Isn't everyone
here really phony?

1482
00:56:56,480 --> 00:56:57,815
- I cannot move.

1483
00:57:00,152 --> 00:57:03,087
- [John] That's an unusual
insignia on your ring.

1484
00:57:03,087 --> 00:57:06,892
- An ancient household
going back for centuries.

1485
00:57:06,892 --> 00:57:09,960
- Knights of Columbus?
- Yes, I know.

1486
00:57:11,528 --> 00:57:13,498
- [Joel] You an
Iron Butterfly man?

1487
00:57:13,498 --> 00:57:15,200
- We've been told
to leave. Let's go.

1488
00:57:15,200 --> 00:57:16,400
- Come on, man.

1489
00:57:16,400 --> 00:57:17,635
That Jack Perkins
guy really scares me.

1490
00:57:17,635 --> 00:57:20,405
- I may leave when
he lets me go.

1491
00:57:21,572 --> 00:57:22,773
- [Tom] Tonight
on "Ninja Master",

1492
00:57:22,773 --> 00:57:24,942
Lee Van Cleef and Sho Kosugi

1493
00:57:24,942 --> 00:57:27,778
in a deadly game
of cat and mouse.

1494
00:57:29,547 --> 00:57:31,548
- The old man hired you.

1495
00:57:31,548 --> 00:57:32,817
- I am not for hire.

1496
00:57:32,817 --> 00:57:35,820
- We are all for
hire in dark times.

1497
